**`dbCrtInst(cv: emyDesign, point: emyPointF, master: emyDesign=None, lib: emyString=””, cell: emyString=””, view: emyString=”layout”, inst: emyString=””, orient: emyString=”R0”, justify: emyString=”origin”, rowPitch: float=0.0, colPitch: float=0.0, rows: int=1, cols: int=1, mag: float=1, angle: float=0, params: vector1D_emyString=None) -\> emyInst`**

This command is used to create an instance. It returns a figure identifier when the instance is created.

Parameters
**cv**emyDesign
It specifies cell view identifier.

**point**emyPointF
It specifies origin or instance.

**master**emyDesign, optional
It specifies the instance master identifier.

**lib**emyString, optional
It specifies the library name of instance. If it is not specified, the library of cell view identifier will be used.

**cell**emyString, optional
It specifies the cell name of Instance.

**view**emyString, optional
It specifies the view name of instance.

**inst**emyString, optional
It specifies the name of instance.

**orient**emyString, optional
It specifies orient of instance. Available values include R0, R90, R180, R270, MY, MYR90, MX, MXR90.

**justify**emyString, optional
It specifies justification of instance. Available values include upperLeft, centerLeft, lowerLeft, upperCenter, centerCenter, lowerCenter, upperRight, centerRight, lowerRight, origin.

**rowPitch**float, optional
It specifies the Y coordinate pitch of instance array.

**colPitch**float, optional
It specifies the X coordinate pitch of instance array.

**rows**int, optional
It specifies the row number of instance array.

**cols**int, optional
It specifies the column number of instance array.

**mag**float, optional
It specifies the magnify of instance.

**angle**float, optional
It specifies the angle that the instance rotates around its master’s origin.

**params**vector1D_emyString, optional
Tip

This parameter supports python built-in type, refer to here for more details.

It specifies the parameter array of parameterized cell instance.

Returns
emyInst

