  "api_descriptions": "# emyScalarTerm\n\n*class* `emyScalarTerm`(*\\*args*, *\\*\\*kwargs*)\n**Inheritance diagram for emyScalarTerm:**\n\nThe emyScalarTerm class implements a scalar terminal on an `emyBlock`. Scalar terminals are single bit and have a name without an index. A scalar terminal must be created on a single-bit net, although the net name need not be scalar.\n\nemyScalarTerm objects are always in the block domain. emyScalarTerms can be purely physical terminals which are only in the block hierarchy, or they can be cross-domain terminals corresponding directly to an `emyModScalarTerm` in the module domain and an `emyOccScalarTerm` in the occurrence domain.\n\n*static* `create`(*net*, *name*, *type=2*, *view=0*)\n**`create(net: emyBitNet, name: emyScalarName, type: emyTermType = emcInputOutputTermType, view: emyBlockDomainVisibility = emcInheritFromTopBlock) -\\> emyScalarTerm`**\n\nCreates an emyScalarTerm object on the specified net. It will check the net to verify its validity.\n\nParameters\n**net :**\nThe bit net to check.\n\n**name :**\nThe scalar terminal name.\n\n**type :**\nThe type of terminal.\n\n**view :**\nSets this net’s visibility in the module domain.\n\nReturns\nThe created scalar terminal object.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotCreateTermWithImplicitNet :\n\nemcTermExists :\n\nemcTermMemberExists :\n\nemcScalarTermNameMatchesBusBaseName :\n\nemcImplicitModuleTermExists :\n\nemcInvalidHierTermName :\n\nemcTermNetMustBeInUniqueOccHier :\n\nemcOverridingTermAlreadyExist :\n\nemcCannotBlockOverrideNetSignalType :\n\nemcPhysOnlyTermNetMustBeInSameOcc :\n\n*static* `find`(*block*, *name*)\n**`find(block: emyBlock, name: emyScalarName) -\\> emyScalarTerm`**\n\nFinds the specified block for a scalarTerm with the specified name.\n\nParameters\n**block :**\nThe block to find.\n\n**name :**\nFills out the scalar terminal name.\n\nReturns\nemyScalarTerm :\nIf found, returns the emyScalarTerm object. Otherwise, returns None.\n\n`getName`(*\\*args*)\n**`getName(name: emyName)`**\n\n**`getName(ns: emyNameSpace, name: emyString)`**\n\nHint\n\nThis function is overloaded. For further information, see below.\n\n- **`getName(name: emyName)`**\n\n  > With the name of this terminal, this function fills up *name*.\n\n- **`getName(ns: emyNameSpace, name: emyString)`**\n\n  > With the name of this terminal mapped to the supplied nameSpace, this function fills in *name*.\n\n*static* `isValidName`(*block*, *name*)\n**`isValidName(block: emyBlock, name: emyScalarName) -\\> emyBoolean`**\n\nReturns a boolean value that represents whether specified name is legal. And also returns True if the name corresponds to a scalarTerm which was hidden but not overridden.\n\nParameters\n**block :**\nThe block to find.\n\n**name :**\nThe name of the scalar terminal to return.\n\n`setName`(*name*)\n**`setName(name: emyScalarName)`**\n\nSets this terminal name to the new name.\n\nParameters\n**name :**\nThe new terminal name.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotSetNameOfImplicitTerm :\n\nemcCannotSetNameOfTermInBundleTerm :\n\nemcScalarTermNameMatchesBusBaseName :\n\nemcTermExists :",
  "category": "emyDatabase"
}"},{"type":"text","text":"{
