  "api_descriptions": "# emyTerm\n\n*class* `emyTerm`(*\\*args*, *\\*\\*kwargs*)\n**Inheritance diagram for emyTerm:**\n\nThe abstract base class for all scalar and multi-bit terminals is called emyTerm. The logical connection points for a block are represented by terminals. The physical connecting points are represented by the pins connected to the terminals. In a design hierarchy, the nets connected to the terminals are logically exported through the terminals to the subsequent higher level.\n\nEven if there is nothing else connected to the net, every terminal must have one.\n\nA collection of logical connections to import or export from the block are represented by multi-bit terminals. The terminals may be composed of busTerms, which have a single root name and an index range, or they may be composed of bundleTerms, a more intricate arrangement of terminals. Names for multi-bit terminals may be redundant. The busTerms “addr\\<2:0\\>” and “addr\\<9:0\\>” for instance, are permissible as long as the overlapping bits are linked to the same nets.\n\nA busTermDef controls all busTerms that share the same root name. The busTermDef keeps track of any linked busTerms, busTerms with the same base name, and associated busTermBits, including their least and most significant bits.\n\nIf they do not already exist, BusTermBits are automatically produced for each bit of a busTerm. Applications performing salaried connection traversal of the data can use BusTermBits.\n\nScalarTerms and busTerms may both be found in bundle terms. Along with the bundleTerm itself, the component scalarTerms and busTermBits are also formed automatically when a bundleTerm is constructed. All terminal objects that are generated automatically are regarded as *implicit*.\n\nTerminals have names linked with them. The various terminal objects employ the `emyScalarName`, `emyVectorBitName`, `emyVectorName`, and `emyBundleName` objects in addition to the basic `emyName` object to take and return names. The mapping of names from one nameSpace to another is controlled by these name objects. A name from the CDBA nameSpace, for instance, can be used to build a terminal. The terminal name in the Verilog nameSpace can be immediately retrieved by another application from the database.\n\nemyTerm objects are in the block domain at all times. emyTerms can be cross-domain terminals that immediately correspond to an `emyModTerm` in the module domain and an `emyOccTerm` in the occurrence domain, or they can be physical-only terminals that are only present in the block hierarchy.\n\n*static* `create`(*net*, *name*, *termType=2*, *view=0*)\n**`create(net: emyNet, name: emyName, termType: emyTermType = emcInputOutputTermType, view: emyBlockDomainVisibility = emcInheritFromTopBlock) -\\> emyTerm`**\n\nFor the given net, this function builds a terminal. This function generates the relevant terminal from a name object that is sent to it. The view parameter for a hidden term has to be set to emcExcludeFromModuleDomain.\n\nParameters\n**net:**\nThe terminal’s connection net\n\n**name:**\nThe terminal’s name that will be created\n\n**type:**\nThe kind of terminal to construct\n\n**view:**\nIndicates whether or not this phrase appears in the module domain\n\nReturns\nThe emyTerm pointer\n\nRaises\nemcTermExists:\n\nemcScalarTermNameMatchesBusBaseName:\n\nemcBusTermBaseNameMatchesScalarName:\n\nemcNetTermWidthMismatch:\n\nemcTermMemberExists:\n\nemcCannotCreateTermWithImplicitNet:\n\nemcImplicitModuleTermExists:\n\nemcInvalidHierTermName:\n\nemcInvalidTermName:\n\nemcTermNetMustBeInUniqueOccHier:\n\nemcOverridingTermAlreadyExist:\n\nemcPhysOnlyTermNetMustBeInSameOcc:\n\nemcCannotBlockOverrideNetSignalType:\n\n`destroy`()\n**`destroy()`**\n\nBy destroying it, this function deletes the terminal from the database. An exception will be raised if this function is called on a phrase that is not explicit.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotDestroyImplicitTerm :\n\n*static* `find`(*\\*args*)\n**`find(block: emyBlock, name: emyName) -\\> emyTerm`**\n\n**`find(block: emyBlock, position: emyUInt4) -\\> emyTerm`**\n\nHint\n\nThis function is overloaded. For further information, see below.\n\n- **`find(block: emyBlock, name: emyName) -\\> emyTerm`**\n\nThis function looks for a terminal with the supplied *name* in the block that is specified. If found, the terminal is delivered. If not, None is shown instead. A hidden terminal is never returned by this method.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\nblock:\nThe terminal block to look for\n\nname:\nThe matching terminal’s name\n\n[\\*\\*](#id2)Returns:[\\*\\*](#id4)getNet\n\nThe emyTerm to look for\n\n- **`find(block: emyBlock, position: emyUInt4) -\\> emyTerm`**\n\nThis function looks for a terminal allocated to the provided *position* in the block that is specified. If found, the terminal is delivered. If not, None is shown instead. A hidden terminal is never returned by this method.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\nblock:\nThe terminal block to look for\n\nposition:\nThe terminal’s location should correspond to\n\nReturns:\nemyTerm to look for\n\n`getBit`(*bitIndex*)\n**`getBit(bitIndex: emyUInt4) -\\> emyBitTerm`**\n\nA pointer to the terminal that corresponds to the specified *bitIndex* bit of this terminal is returned by this function. This function returns this terminal for single-bit terminals. For multi-bit terminals, a single-bit terminal or a busTermBit, depending on whether the terminal is a busTerm or a bundleTerm, is returned. A pointer to the `emyOccBitTerm` , which corresponds to the domain in which the multibit occTerm has a reflection, is returned by this function.\n\nRaises\nemcInvalidTermIndex:\n\n`getConnRoutes`()\n**`getConnRoutes() -\\> emyCollection_emyRoute_emyTerm`**\n\nA list of routes that are linked to this terminal is returned by this function. This terminal serves as either the startConn, endConn, or both for each route in the collection.\n\n*static* `getMaxPosition`(*block*)\n**`getMaxPosition(block: emyBlock) -\\> emyUInt4`**\n\nThe highest position a terminal has in the *block* that has been given is returned by this function. The value emcNoneIndex is returned if there are no terminals in the block or if no position has a terminal allocated to it.\n\nParameters\n**block:**\nThe block to report the top allocated terminal position comes from\n\n`getName`(*\\*args*)\n**`getName(name: emyName)`**\n\n**`getName(ns: emyNameSpace, name: emyString)`**\n\nHint\n\nThis function is overloaded. For further information, see below.\n\n- **`getName(name: emyName)`**\n\n  > With the name of this terminal, this function fills up *name*.\n\n- **`getName(ns: emyNameSpace, name: emyString)`**\n\n  > With the name of this terminal mapped to the supplied nameSpace, this function fills in *name*.\n\n`getNet`(*preferred=False*)\n**`getNet(preferred: emyBoolean = False) -\\> emyNet`**\n\nThe net that this terminal is connected to is returned by this function. The preferred equivalent net connected to the net will be returned if *preferred* is *true*.\n\nParameters\n**preferred:**\nif the desired equivalent should be returned\n\nReturns\nThe emyNet that this terminal is connected\n\n`getNumBits`()\n**`getNumBits() -\\> emyUInt4`**\n\nThe number of bits in this terminal is returned by this function.\n\n`getOccTerm`()\n**`getOccTerm() -\\> emyOccTerm`**\n\nThis method returns the term that appears in the top occurrence of the design that contains the block term and is a reflection of it.\n\n`getOccTerms`(*top*)\n**`getOccTerms(top: emyOccurrence) -\\> emyCollection_emyOccTerm_emyTerm`**\n\nA collection of occTerms on this term in the specified top occurrence is returned by this function.\n\nParameters\n**top:**\nThe top occurrence\n\n`getPins`()\n**`getPins() -\\> emyCollection_emyPin_emyTerm`**\n\nThe collection of pins connected to this terminal is returned by this method.\n\n`getPosition`()\n**`getPosition() -\\> emyUInt4`**\n\nThe location that this terminal is allocated to is returned by this function. If this terminal hasn’t been given a position, the value emcNoneIndex is returned.\n\n`getTermType`()\n**`getTermType() -\\> emyTermType`**\n\nThe terminal type of this terminal is returned by this function.\n\n`isImplicit`()\n**`isImplicit() -\\> emyBoolean`**\n\nWhether this terminal is implicit is indicated by the boolean result returned by this function. As part of the explicit establishment of a multi-bit terminal, the database automatically creates an implicit terminal.\n\n`isInterface`()\n**`isInterface() -\\> emyBoolean`**\n\nIf the terminal is an interface terminal, this method returns a boolean value. A terminal that has been deliberately constructed by an application executing one of the create functions on objects descended from emyTerm is referred to as an interface terminal. The interface to the block in which they are found is defined by explicitly built terminals.\n\nIt should be noted that a scalarized interface terminal is still regarded as an interface terminal. After scalarization, implementation data may be added to the resultant bitTerms, but the interface terminal is kept around as a reminder of how the interface was once designed. The interface terminal may be deleted as a result of additional updates to the block, which would indicate that the block’s interface has really changed.\n\n*static* `isValidName`(*net*, *name*)\n**`isValidName(net: emyNet, name: emyName) -\\> emyBoolean`**\n\nIf the specified *name*, connected to the specified *net*, is valid for a new emyTerm object, this function will return a boolean value. Additionally, if the name matches a phrase that was hidden but not replaced, this function will return True.\n\n`moveToNet`(*net*)\n**`moveToNet(net: emyNet)`**\n\nThe specified *net* is where this terminal is moved by this function.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotModifyImplicitTerm:\n\nemcCannotMoveToImplicitNet:\n\nemcCannotMoveToBlockOnlyNet:\n\nemcCannotTransferNetWithTerm:\n\nemcMoveToNetNotInSameBlock:\n\nemcTermNetMustBeInUniqueOccHier:\n\nemcTermMustJoinSameNet:\n\n`scalarize`()\n**`scalarize()`**\n\nTo accommodate implementation data like pins and routes, this method makes sure that the bitTerms linked to this terminal have been promoted to the explicit state.\n\nThis function ensures that all component bitTerms are promoted to the explicit state if this terminal is a multibit terminal. In order to prevent implementation data from being connected to the multibit terminal, it is subsequently demoted to the implicit state. The accompanying implementation data is deleted from a terminal when it is demoted to the implicit state.\n\nA multi-bit terminal’s status as an interface terminal (a terminal that was specifically built specifies the initial interface for its associated block) is unaffected by the terminal’s degradation.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotScalarizeImplicitTerm:\n\n`setIsInterface`(*isInterface*)\n**`setIsInterface(isInterface: emyBoolean)`**\n\nThis function modifies the terminal’s isInterface value. Please refer to `isInterface` for further details.\n\nParameters\n**isInterface:**\nTo set or unset the isInterface value, use true or false.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotSetIsInterfaceOfImplicitTerm:\n\n`setPosition`(*position*)\n**`setPosition(position: emyUInt4)`**\n\nThis function moves or moves this terminal to the place that is supplied. Assigning a location to an implicit terminal or a terminal that is only accessible to the block domain is incorrect. A spot that is designated for another terminal is similarly incorrect.\n\nParameters\n**position:**\nThe location where the terminal should be placed.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotSetPositionOfImplicitTerm:\n\nemcCannotSetPositionOfBlockOnlyTerm:\n\nemcTermPositionAlreadyTaken:\n\n`setTermType`(*termType*)\n**`setTermType(termType: emyTermType)`**\n\nThe terminal type for this terminal is modified by this function.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotSetBusTermBitTermType:\n\n`unsetPosition`()\n**`unsetPosition()`**\n\nBy clearing the position that this terminal is allocated to, this operation makes room for another terminal to be placed there. If this terminal doesn’t have a position allocated right now, nothing happens.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotSetPositionOfImplicitTerm:\n\nemcCannotSetPositionOfBlockOnlyTerm:\n\nTip\n\nMore properties are supported in this class, refer to here for more details.\n\n---\n\n## 补充说明（通过测试验证）\n\n# emyTerm API 测试经验总结与丰富描述\n\n## 1. API 功能概述\n\n`emyTerm` 类是 pyAether 中所有标量和多位终端的抽象基类。终端表示块的逻辑连接点，物理连接点由连接到终端的引脚表示。在设计层次结构中，连接到终端的网络通过终端逻辑导出到后续更高级别。\n\n### 主要功能\n- 创建和销毁终端\n- 查找终端（通过名称或位置）\n- 获取终端属性（名称、网络、位置、类型等）\n- 管理终端位置和类型\n- 处理隐式和显式终端\n- 标量化多比特终端\n\n## 2. 参数使用技巧\n\n### 2.1 终端类型 (emyTermType)\n终端类型使用 `emyTermType` 类创建，支持以下类型：\n\n| 类型常量 | 值 | 描述 |\n|---------|-----|------|\n| `emcInputTermType` | 0 | 输入终端 |\n| `emcOutputTermType` | 1 | 输出终端 |\n| `emcInputOutputTermType` | 2 | 输入输出终端（默认） |\n| `emcSwitchTermType` | 3 | 开关终端 |\n| `emcJumperTermType` | 4 | 跳线终端 |\n| `emcUnusedTermType` | 5 | 未使用终端 |\n| `emcTristateTermType` | 6 | 三态终端 |\n\n**使用示例：**\n```python\nimport pyAether as pa\n\n# 创建终端类型对象\ninput_type = pa.emyTermType(\"input\")  # 使用字符串\noutput_type = pa.emyTermType(\"output\")\nio_type = pa.emyTermType(\"inputOutput\")\n\n# 或使用常量\ninput_type_const = pa.emcInputTermType  # 值为 0\noutput_type_const = pa.emcOutputTermType  # 值为 1\n```\n\n### 2.2 名称对象 (emyName)\n创建终端时需要 `emyName` 对象，必须指定名称空间：\n\n```python\n# 创建 CDBA 名称空间\ncdba_ns = pa.emyCdbaNS()\n\n# 创建名称对象\nterm_name = pa.emyName(cdba_ns, \"my_terminal\")\nnet_name = pa.emyName(cdba_ns, \"my_net\")\n```\n\n### 2.3 创建终端\n创建终端需要网络、名称和终端类型：\n\n```python\n# 基本创建（使用默认参数）\nterm = pa.emyTerm.create(net, term_name, term_type)\n\n# 使用默认终端类型（emcInputOutputTermType）\nterm = pa.emyTerm.create(net, term_name)  # termType 默认为 2\n\n# 使用 emyTermCreateWhenNeeded（带错误消息参数）\nterm = pa.emyTermCreateWhenNeeded(net, term_name, term_type, errMsg=None)\n```\n\n## 3. 返回值详细说明\n\n### 3.1 主要方法返回值\n\n| 方法 | 返回值类型 | 说明 |\n|------|-----------|------|\n| `create()` | `emyTerm` | 返回新创建的终端对象指针 |\n| `find()` | `emyTerm` 或 `None` | 找到则返回终端，否则返回 None |\n| `getBit(bitIndex)` | `emyBitTerm` | 返回对应位的终端 |\n| `getNet()` | `emyNet` | 返回终端连接的网络 |\n| `getNumBits()` | `emyUInt4` | 返回终端位数（标量终端为1） |\n| `getPosition()` | `emyUInt4` | 返回终端位置，未设置返回 `emcNoneIndex` |\n| `getTermType()` | `emyTermType` | 返回终端类型对象 |\n| `isImplicit()` | `emyBoolean` | 返回是否为隐式终端 |\n| `isInterface()` | `emyBoolean` | 返回是否为接口终端 |\n\n### 3.2 特殊返回值\n- `emcNoneIndex`: 表示未设置位置的常量值\n- 隐式终端：自动创建的多比特终端组件\n- 接口终端：显式创建的终端，定义块的接口\n\n## 4. 常见错误和解决方法\n\n### 4.1 名称空间错误\n**错误：** `Wrong number or type of arguments for overloaded function 'new_emyName'`\n**原因：** 创建 `emyName` 时未提供名称空间参数\n**解决：** 必须使用名称空间创建名称对象\n```python\n# 错误：pa.emyName(\"test\")  # 缺少名称空间参数\n# 正确：\ncdba_ns = pa.emyCdbaNS()\nname = pa.emyName(cdba_ns, \"test\")\n```\n\n### 4.2 无效终端类型\n**错误：** `SystemError: Invalid termType name`\n**原因：** 使用了无效的终端类型名称\n**解决：** 使用有效的终端类型名称或常量\n```python\n# 错误：pa.emyTermType(\"invalid_type\")\n# 正确：pa.emyTermType(\"input\") 或 pa.emcInputTermType\n```\n\n### 4.3 设计上下文缺失\n**错误：** 各种方法调用失败\n**原因：** 未在有效的设计上下文中操作\n**解决：** 确保已打开设计并获取块和网络对象\n```python\n# 需要先有设计、块和网络\ndesign = pa.aeOpenDesign(\"lib\", \"cell\", \"view\", \"edit\", False)\nblock = design.getTopBlock()\nnet = pa.emyNet.create(block, net_name)\nterm = pa.emyTerm.create(net, term_name, term_type)\n```\n\n### 4.4 重复终端名称\n**错误：** `emcTermExists` 异常\n**原因：** 尝试创建已存在的终端\n**解决：** 使用 `isValidName()` 检查或使用 `find()` 查找现有终端\n```python\n# 检查名称是否有效\nis_valid = pa.emyTerm.isValidName(net, term_name)\nif is_valid:\n    term = pa.emyTerm.create(net, term_name, term_type)\n```\n\n## 5. 最佳实践和常用场景\n\n### 5.1 终端创建流程\n```python\nimport pyAether as pa\n\n# 1. 初始化 Aether\npa.emyInitAether(\"-adv\")\n\n# 2. 打开设计\ndesign = pa.aeOpenDesign(\"mylib\", \"mycell\", \"layout\", \"edit\", False)\n\n# 3. 获取块\nblock = design.getTopBlock()\n\n# 4. 创建名称空间和名称\ncdba_ns = pa.emyCdbaNS()\nnet_name = pa.emyName(cdba_ns, \"data_bus\")\nterm_name = pa.emyName(cdba_ns, \"data_input\")\n\n# 5. 创建网络\nnet = pa.emyNet.create(block, net_name)\n\n# 6. 创建终端类型\nterm_type = pa.emyTermType(\"input\")  # 或 pa.emcInputTermType\n\n# 7. 创建终端\nterm = pa.emyTerm.create(net, term_name, term_type)\n```\n\n### 5.2 终端查询和管理\n```python\n# 查找终端\nfound_term = pa.emyTerm.find(block, term_name)\n\n# 设置和获取位置\nterm.setPosition(10)\nposition = term.getPosition()\n\n# 检查终端属性\nis_implicit = term.isImplicit()  # 隐式终端（自动创建）\nis_interface = term.isInterface()  # 接口终端（显式创建）\n\n# 获取连接的网络\nconnected_net = term.getNet()\n\n# 获取终端类型\nterm_type_obj = term.getTermType()\ntype_name = term_type_obj.getName()  # \"input\", \"output\", 等\n```\n\n### 5.3 多比特终端处理\n```python\n# 获取终端位数\nnum_bits = term.getNumBits()\n\n# 获取特定位的终端（对于多比特终端）\nif num_bits > 1:\n    for i in range(num_bits):\n        bit_term = term.getBit(i)\n        # 处理每个位终端\n```\n\n### 5.4 错误处理\n```python\ntry:\n    term = pa.emyTerm.create(net, term_name, term_type)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"创建终端失败: {e}\")\n    # 检查常见错误\n    if \"emcTermExists\" in str(e):\n        print(\"终端已存在\")\n    elif \"emcInvalidTermName\" in str(e):\n        print(\"无效的终端名称\")\n    elif \"emcNetTermWidthMismatch\" in str(e):\n        print(\"网络与终端宽度不匹配\")\n```\n\n## 6. 测试经验总结\n\n### 6.1 成功验证的功能\n1. **终端类型创建**：成功创建各种终端类型对象\n2. **常量使用**：验证了所有终端类型常量的值\n3. **API方法存在性**：确认了所有主要方法都存在\n4. **错误处理**：验证了无效输入的异常处理\n\n### 6.2 遇到的挑战\n1. **设计上下文依赖**：大多数 `emyTerm` 方法需要有效的设计、块和网络对象\n2. **名称空间要求**：`emyName` 对象必须使用名称空间创建\n3. **初始化要求**：需要先调用 `pa.emyInitAether(\"-adv\")` 初始化环境\n\n### 6.3 测试限制\n由于测试环境限制，无法完整测试以下功能：\n- 实际终端创建（需要设计上下文）\n- 网络和块的创建\n- 终端与网络的连接验证\n- 位置管理功能\n- 隐式/显式终端转换\n\n### 6.4 建议的完整测试环境\n要完整测试 `emyTerm` API，需要：\n1. 有效的工艺库（如 TECHLIB）\n2. 打开或创建的设计\n3. 块对象\n4. 网络对象\n5. 正确的名称空间设置\n\n## 7. API 使用注意事项\n\n### 7.1 设计上下文\n- 所有 `emyTerm` 操作都需要在设计上下文中进行\n- 必须先有有效的 `emyNet` 对象才能创建终端\n- 终端始终位于块域中\n\n### 7.2 名称管理\n- 终端名称通过 `emyName` 对象管理\n- 支持跨名称空间的名称映射\n- 多比特终端名称可能重复（如 \"addr<2:0>\" 和 \"addr<9:0>\"）\n\n### 7.3 隐式与显式终端\n- **隐式终端**：自动创建的多比特终端组件\n- **显式终端**：通过 `create()` 方法手动创建\n- 隐式终端不能直接修改或销毁\n- 使用 `scalarize()` 方法将隐式终端提升为显式状态\n\n### 7.4 终端位置\n- 位置是终端在块中的索引\n- 使用 `setPosition()` 和 `getPosition()` 管理\n- `unsetPosition()` 清除位置分配\n- `getMaxPosition()` 获取块中最大位置\n\n### 7.5 错误代码\n了解常见异常有助于调试：\n- `emcTermExists`: 终端已存在\n- `emcInvalidTermName`: 无效的终端名称\n- `emcCannotDestroyImplicitTerm`: 不能销毁隐式终端\n- `emcCannotSetPositionOfImplicitTerm`: 不能设置隐式终端位置\n- `emcTermPositionAlreadyTaken`: 终端位置已被占用\n\n## 8. 性能考虑\n\n1. **批量操作**：创建多个终端时考虑性能影响\n2. **位置管理**：频繁的位置更改可能影响性能\n3. **隐式终端**：自动创建的隐式终端有性能优势\n4. **查找优化**：使用 `find()` 方法时考虑块中终端数量\n\n## 9. 扩展功能\n\n### 9.1 与其他对象交互\n- 终端与引脚 (`emyPin`) 连接\n- 终端与路由 (`emyRoute`) 关联\n- 通过 `getOccTerm()` 获取出现域中的对应终端\n\n### 9.2 高级用法\n- 创建总线终端 (`emyBusTerm`)\n- 创建束终端 (`emyBundleTerm`)\n- 处理跨域终端（块域、模块域、出现域）\n\n## 10. 结论\n\n`emyTerm` API 提供了强大的终端管理功能，支持从简单标量终端到复杂多比特终端的各种用例。正确使用需要理解设计上下文、名称空间管理和终端生命周期。通过遵循最佳实践和正确处理错误，可以有效地在 pyAether 应用程序中集成终端功能。\n\n**关键要点：**\n1. 始终使用正确的名称空间创建 `emyName` 对象\n2. 在设计上下文中操作终端\n3. 区分隐式和显式终端\n4. 合理管理终端位置\n5. 使用 `isValidName()` 预先验证名称\n6. 正确处理多比特终端场景\n",
  "category": "emyDatabase"
}"},{"type":"text","text":"{
