- **`open(libNameIn: emyScalarName, cellNameIn: emyScalarName, viewNameIn: emyScalarName, mode: emyChar) -\> emyDesign`**

  > Open the design with the specified library, cell, and view name with the specified access mode. If successful, return the design. This version opens the design using the viewType attribute of the emyViewType object pointed to by viewType.
  >
  > This parameter transfer method can be used to open an existing design for reading or modifying. If this open function is called to create (write) a new design, an exception will be thrown because each design needs the specification of viewType when it is created.
  >
  > When you open a library for ‘w’rite, ‘a’ppend, or ‘A’ppend with this function, the library container is temporarily locked. If another user attempts to use `open` to ‘w’rite, ‘a’ppend, or ‘A’ppend to the library, an emcDesignCannotGetWriteAccess exception is thrown. This behavior protects against\*another\*process opening the same library for write or append access.
  >
  > When you open a database in ‘w’rite mode and then save the database, the mode changes to ‘a’ppend. When you open a database in ‘A’ppend mode and then save that database, the mode changes to ‘a’ppend.
  >
  > After opening the library for ‘w’rite, ‘a’ppend, or ‘A’ppend, EmpyDatabase creates a database file and a lock file for you. After this point, the access to the library container is once again opened for ‘w’rite, ‘a’ppend, or ‘A’ppend mode to other users. However, anyone attempting to access the locked database file will get an emcCannotLockDatabase exception.
