  "api_descriptions": "# emyArray_T\n\nThe name “emyArray_T” is an abstract representation of a series of flattened template classes that provide a dynamic array in c++ implementations. Actually, There is no class named “emyArray_T” in pyAether.\n\nUses emyArray_emyString as an example to describe generic interfaces of all emyArray concrete classes, and interfaces of other concrete types are exactly the same as it.\n\n*class* `emyArray_emyString`(*\\*args*)\nThis class is a utility class that implements an array of emyString.\n\n`__eq__`(*other*)\nReturn self==value.\n\n`append`(*\\*args*)\nThis function appends the specified emyString element to the end of this array. This function will increase the size of the array if necessary and will increment the number of elements in the array.\n\n`equal`(*arrayIn*)\nReturns a boolean indicating whether this array is equivalent to the specified array.\n\n`find`(*element*)\n**`find(element: emyString) -\\> emyUInt4`**\n\nFinds this array for the specified element. The position of the element in the array is returned if found. Otherwise, the value oacNullIndex is returned.\n\nParameters\n**element**emyString\nThe element to search for in this array.\n\n`get`(*index*)\n**`get(index: emyUInt4) -\\> emyString`**\n\nReturns the emyString element in this array at the specified index.\n\nParameters\n**index**emyUInt4\nSpecifies the index element in the array to access.\n\nReturns\n**out**emyString\nThe emyString element.\n\nNotes\n\nThis function does not check whether the index is valid.\n\n`getElements`()\n**`getElements() -\\> emyUInt4`**\n\nReturns a const pointer to the elements in array.\n\n`getNumElements`()\n**`getNumElements() -\\> emyUInt4`**\n\nReturns the number of elements this array contains.\n\n`getSize`()\n**getSize() -\\>emyUInt4**\n\nReturns the allocated size of this array. The number of elements may be less than the allocated size of the array.\n\n`remove`(*element*)\n**`remove(element: emyString)`**\n\nRemoves the specified element from this array, shifting the remaining elements up to fill in the gap. The number of elements is decremented accordingly.\n\nParameters\n**element**emyString\nThe element to remove from this array.\n\n`set`(*arrayIn*, *numElementsIn*)\n**`set(arrayIn: emyArray_emyString, numElementsIn: emyUInt4)`**\n\nCopies numElements from the specified another array to this array. The size of this array is set to numElements.\n\nParameters\n**arrayIn**emyArray_emyString\nthe another array to copy.\n\n**numElementsIn**emyUInt4\nnumber of elements to copy.\n\n`setNumElements`(*n*)\n**`setNumElements(n: emyUInt4)`**\n\nSets the number of elements in this array to the specified n value.\n\nNotes\n\nThe specified value is not checked against the actual size of the array. This is normally used when an application first sets the size of the array, fills it in, and then sets the number of elements the array contains.\n\n`setSize`(*newSize*, *saveElements=False*)\n**`setSize(newSize: emyUInt4 :emyBoolean=False)`**\n\nResizes this array to contain the specified newSize number of elements. If saveElements is False, this array is not initialized. If true, the original data is preserved. If newSize is less than numObjs, all of the data will not be preserved.\n\nParameters\n**newSize**emyUInt4\nThe new size of the array.\n\n**saveElements**emyBoolean, optional\nIndicates whether the resized array will be reinitialized (saveElements = False) or the current data (up to and including the number of elements specified by newSize) will be preserved (saveElements = True).\n\n`sort`(*compare*)\nSorts the elements of the array in-place.\n\n`sort_wrapper`(*handler*)\n\n## All concrete emyArray class\n\nAll concrete emyArray class list in emyDatabase module:\n\n| Class Name                       |     |\n|----------------------------------|-----|\n| emyArray_emyAntennaArea          |     |\n| emyArray_emyBox                  |     |\n| emyArray_emyDMAttr               |     |\n| emy