  "api_descriptions": "# MdeSetting\n\n*class* `MdeSetting`(*\\*args*, *\\*\\*kwargs*)\nAn MdeSetting object represents the setting information of an `MdeSession` object. It can be seen as an in-memory mirror of the setting file of an MDE state. Setting information, such as project directory and outputs, can be read or modified through this class. Any modifications that occur to an MdeSetting object can be reflected in the next simulation run launched by `MdeSession.netlistAndRun`.\n\n`addModelFile`(*modelFile*)\n**`addModelFile(modelFile: std::string)`**\n\nAdds a model file for Nominal Corner. This is the same as one adds a model file in the “Model Setup” table widget. Duplicate model files are allowed.\n\nParameters\n**modelFile**str\nModel file name with relative path to it.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.addModelFile(\"modelFileName\")\n\n`addModelFileForCorners`(*modelFile*)\n**`addModelFileForCorners(modelFile: std::string)`**\n\nAdds a model file for all corners. This is the same as one adds a model file in the “Corner Setup form”. Duplicate model files are allowed.\n\nParameters\n**modelFile**str\nModel file name with relative path to it.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.addModelFileForCorners(\"modelFileName\")\n\n`addParameter`(*paramName*)\n**`addParameter(paramName: std::string)`**\n\nAdd a parameter for Nominal Corner. If the parameter has already been added, nothing will happen.\n\nParameters\n**paramName**str\nNew parameter name to be added.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.addParameter(\"parameterName\")\n\n`addParameterForCorners`(*paramName*)\n**`addParameterForCorners(paramName: std::string)`**\n\nAdd a parameter for corners. If the parameter has already been added, nothing will happen.\n\nParameters\n**paramName**str\nNew parameter name to be added.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.addParameterForCorners(\"parameterName\")\n\n`addSpeOutput`(*output*)\n**`addSpeOutput(output: MdeSpeOutput) -\\> bool`**\n\nAdd an `MdeSpeOutput` to the MdeSetting object. If the MdeSetting object is not from a Spectre mode MdeSession, or another output with the same name already exists, the output will not be added.\n\nParameters\n**output**MdeSpeOutput\nThe `MdeSpeOutput` object.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, the output will be added and the method will returns True. Otherwise, it will return False. On failure, check the error message by calling `MdeSetting.lastError`. Typical failure scenarios include the corresponding `MdeSession` object having been closed and an output with the same output name already existing.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.addSpeOutput(MdeSpeOutput(name=\"corner_max\", expr=\"max(VT(SUB),overall=t)\",\n    ... exprType=\"Expression\", evalType=\"Corners\", save=False, plot=True))\n\n`cornerExists`(*name*)\n**`cornerExists(name: std::string) -\\> bool`**\n\nChecks whether the specified corner exists.\n\nParameters\n**name**str\nName of a corner.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nReturns true if the specified corner exists and false otherwise.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.cornerExists(\"C5\")\n    true\n\n`createCorner`(*name*)\n**`createCorner(name: std::string) -\\> MdeSpeCorner`**\n\nCreates new corner with the specified name, saves new corresponding MdeSpeCorner object in internal array and returns this new MdeSpeCorner object. If the corner already exists, returns the existing MdeSpeCorner object.\n\nParameters\n**name**str\nName of new corner to be created.\n\nReturns\n**out**MdeSpeCorner\nNew MdeSpeCorner object.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> mdeCorner = setting.createCorner(\"C2\")\n\n`deleteCustom`(*key*)\n**`deleteCustom(key: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nDelete the specified custom key in mde setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, the specified custom key and it’s value removed from mde setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.attachToGui(pyScript.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setCustom(\"keyword1\", \"value1\")\n    >>> setting.setCustom(\"keyword2\", \"value2\")\n    >>> setting.deleteCustom(\"keyword2\")\n\n`disableAcAnalysis`()\n**`disableAcAnalysis() -\\> bool`**\n\nDisable ac analysis in MDE setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that ac analysis has been disabled in MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.disableAcAnalysis()\n\n`disableCorner`(*name*)\n**`disableCorner(name: std::string)`**\n\nDisables the corner with specified name.\n\nParameters\n**name**str\nName of a corner.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.disableCorner(\"C6\")\n\n`disableDcAnalysis`()\n**`disableDcAnalysis() -\\> bool`**\n\nDisable dc analysis in MDE setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that dc analysis has been disabled in MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.disableDcAnalysis()\n\n`disableNoiseAnalysis`()\n**`disableNoiseAnalysis() -\\> bool`**\n\nDisable noise analysis in MDE setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that noise analysis has been disabled in MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.disableNoiseAnalysis()\n\n`disableOverwrite`()\n**`disableOverwrite() -\\> bool`**\n\nEnable the overwrited result.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True. Otherwise, returns False. Typical failures scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> isSucc = setting.disableOverwrite()\n    >>> if isSucc:\n    ...     print(\"Disables the overwrited result succeeds\")\n    ... else:\n    ...     print(\"Disables the overwrited result failed\")\n    >\n    >>> mde.close()\n\n`disableStbAnalysis`()\n**`disableStbAnalysis() -\\> bool`**\n\nDisable stb analysis in MDE setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that stb analysis has been disabled in MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.disableStbAnalysis()\n\n`disableTranAnalysis`()\n**`disableTranAnalysis() -\\> bool`**\n\nDisable tran analysis in MDE setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that tran analysis has been disabled in MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.disableTranAnalysis()\n\n`enableAcAnalysis`()\n**`enableAcAnalysis() -\\> bool`**\n\nEnable ac analysis in MDE setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that ac analysis has been enabled in MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.enableAcAnalysis()\n\n`enableCorner`(*name*)\n**`enableCorner(name: std::string)`**\n\nEnables the corner with specified name.\n\nParameters\n**name**str\nName of a corner.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.enableCorner(\"C5\")\n\n`enableDcAnalysis`()\n**`enableDcAnalysis() -\\> bool`**\n\nEnable dc analysis in MDE setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that dc analysis has been enabled in MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.enableDcAnalysis()\n\n`enableNoiseAnalysis`()\n**`enableNoiseAnalysis() -\\> bool`**\n\nEnable noise analysis in MDE setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that noise analysis has been enabled in MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.enableNoiseAnalysis()\n\n`enableOverwrite`()\n**`enableOverwrite() -\\> bool`**\n\nEnable the overwrited result.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True. Otherwise, returns False. Typical failures scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> isSucc = setting.enableOverwrite()\n    >>> if isSucc:\n    ...     print(\"Enables the overwrited result succeeds\")\n    ... else:\n    ...     print(\"Enables the overwrited result failed\")\n    >\n    >>> mde.close()\n\n`enableStbAnalysis`()\n**`enableStbAnalysis() -\\> bool`**\n\nEnable stb analysis in MDE setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that stb analysis has been enabled in MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.enableStbAnalysis()\n\n`enableTranAnalysis`()\n**`enableTranAnalysis() -\\> bool`**\n\nEnable tran analysis in MDE setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that tran analysis has been enabled in MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.enableTranAnalysis()\n\n`getAllCustomKeys`()\n**`getAllCustomKeys() -\\> list\\[str\\]`**\n\nGet all custom keys in mde setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**list\\[str\\]\nA list of custom keys stored in mde setting.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.attachToGui(pyScript.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setCustom(\"keyword1\", \"value1\")\n    >>> setting.setCustom(\"keyword2\", \"value2\")\n    >>> setting.getAllCustomKeys()\n\n`getAllSpeCorners`(*expand=False*)\n**`getAllSpeCorners() -\\> Tuple\\[MdeSpeCorner\\]`**\n\nReturn a list of MdeSpeCorner objects representing all the spectre corners.\n\nReturns\n**out**Tuple\\[MdeSpeCorner\\]\nOn success, return a list of MdeSpeCorner objects. If the corresponding MdeSession object has been closed, the MdeSession is not in Spectre mode or there are no spectre corners available, return an empty list.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>>  corners = setting.getAllSpeCorners()\n\n`getAllSpeOutputs`()\n**`getAllSpeOutputs() -\\> Tuple\\[MdeSpeOutput\\]`**\n\nReturn a list of MdeSpeOutput objects representing all the spectre outputs. Add new parameter “spec” in MdeSpeOutput,the default value is empty.\n\nReturns\n**out**Tuple\\[MdeSpeOutput\\]\nReturns the tuple which includes all MdeSpeOutput of the mde session.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> outputs = setting.getAllSpeOutputs()\n\n`getCorner`(*name*)\n**`getCorner(name: std::string) -\\> MdeSpeCorner`**\n\nReturns the corner with the specified name. Returns null if the corner does not exist.\n\nParameters\n**name**str\nName of a corner.\n\nReturns\n**out**MdeSpeCorner\nMdeSpeCorner object.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> mdeCorner3 = setting.getCorner(\"C3\")\n\n`getCustom`(*key*)\n**`getCustom(key: str) -\\> str`**\n\nGet the value of specified custom key in mde setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**str\nIf the specified custom key exists, return the value of specified custom key, otherwise, return empty string.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.attachToGui(pyScript.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setCustom(\"keyword\", \"value\")\n    >>> setting.getCustom(\"keyword\")\n\n`getCustomDigitalSolver`()\n**`getCustomDigitalSolver() -\\> str`**\n\nGet custom digital solver.\n\nReturns\n**out**str\nCustom digital solver name.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setCustomDigitalSolver(\"mysolver\")\n    >>> setting.getCustomDigitalSolver()\n\n`getDesignTopCellView`()\n**`getDesignTopCellView() -\\> list\\[str\\] `**\n\nObtain the lib, cell and view of a schematic view which is already used to open a MdeSession.\n\nReturns\n**out**list\\[str\\]\nOn success, return a tuple of lib, cell and view. Otherwise, return an empty tuple.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> libCellViewList = setting.getDesignTopCellView()\n    >>> if libCellViewList:\n    ...     print(\"obtain lib, cell and view of the schematic succeeds\")\n    ... else:\n    ...     print(\"obtain lib, cell and view of the schematic failed\")\n\n`getDigitalFormat`()\n**`getDigitalFormat() -\\> MdeAlpsCSDigitalFormatEnum`**\n\nGet digital solver format.\n\nReturns\n**out**MdeAlpsCSDigitalFormatEnum\nReturns the corresponding enum value with MdeAlpsCSDigitalFormatEnum. 0:MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_FORMAT_VCD, the current digital solver format is VCD. 1:MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_FORMAT_FSDB, the current digital solver format is FSDB. 2:MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_FORMAT_ERROR, The digital solver format is not defined, or it is a wrong format.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setDigitalFormat(pyScript.MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_FORMAT_VCD)\n    >>> setting.getDigitalFormat()\n\n`getDigitalSolver`()\n**`getDigitalSolver() -\\> MdeAlpsCSDigitalSolverEnum`**\n\nGet digital solver type.\n\nReturns\n**out**MdeAlpsCSDigitalSolverEnum\nReturns the corresponding enum value with MdeAlpsCSDigitalSolverEnum. 0:MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_MS, the current digital solver is MS. 1:MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_NC, the current digital solver is NC. 2:MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_VCS, the current digital solver is VCS. 3:MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_UVS, the current digital solver is UVS. 4:MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_CUSTOM, the current digital solver is custom. 5:MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_ERROR, the digital solver is not defined, or it is a wrong type.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setDigitalSolver(pyScript.MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_MS)\n    >>> setting.getDigitalSolver()\n\n`getDigitalSolverArgs`()\n**`getDigitalSolverArgs() -\\> str`**\n\nGet digital solver arguments.\n\nReturns\n**out**str\nGet digital solver arguments.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setDigitalSolverArgs(\"-args name\")\n    >>> setting.getDigitalSolverArgs()\n\n`getEnabledCornerList`()\n**`getEnabledCornerList() -\\> List\\[str\\]`**\n\nGet a list of all enabled corners. If an enabled corner (such as “C1”) contains parameter sweep, the split corners (“C1_0”, “C1_1”, etc) will be returned.\n\nReturns\n**out**List\\[str\\]\nReturn a list of the enabled corners. If the corresponding MdeSession is already closed or is not in Spectre mode, an empty list will be returned. On failure, check the error message by calling `lastError`.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> corners = setting.getEnabledCornerList()\n    >>> for c in corners:\n    ...     print(c)\n\n`getEnabledSweepList`()\n**`getEnabledSweepList() -\\> List\\[str\\]`**\n\nGet a list of all enabled sweeps, such as \\[“vpd=1,vp=1.2”, “vpd=1,vp=1.3”, “vpd=2,vp=1.2”, “vpd=2,vp=1.3”\\].\n\nReturns\n**out**List\\[str\\]\nReturn a list of all enabled sweeps. If the corresponding MdeSession is closed, or there is no sweep information in the MdeSetting, an empty list will be returned. On failure, check the error message by calling `lastError`.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> sweeps = setting.getEnabledSweepList()\n    >>> for s in sweeps:\n    ...     print(s)\n\n`getModelFiles`()\n**`getModelFiles() -\\> std::vector\\<std::string\\>`**\n\nReturns all the model files for Nominal Corner.\n\nReturns\n**out**List\\[str\\]\nList of all the model file names for Nominal Corner. As model files allow duplication, the same value might appear multiple times.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> model_files = setting.getModelFiles()\n    >>> for mf in model_files:\n    ...     print(mf)\n\n`getModelFilesForCorners`()\n**`getModelFilesForCorners() -\\> std::vector\\<std::string\\>`**\n\nReturns all the model files for corners.\n\nReturns\n**out**List\\[str\\]\nList of all the model file names for corners. As model files allow duplication, the same value might appear multiple times.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> model_files = setting.getModelFilesForCorners()\n    >>> for mf in model_files:\n    ...     print(mf)\n\n`getNetlistFormat`()\n**`getNetlistFormat() -\\> MdeNetlistFormatEnum`**\n\nGet netlist format.\n\nReturns\n**out**MdeNetlistFormatEnum\nReturns the corresponding enum value with MdeNetlistFormatEnum. 0:MDE_NETLIST_FORMAT_HSPICE, the current netlist format is HSpice. 1:MDE_NETLIST_FORMAT_PSPICE, the current netlist format is PSpice. 2:MDE_NETLIST_FORMAT_SPECTRE, the current netlist format is Spectre.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.getNetlistFormat()\n\n`getNetlistViewList`()\n**`getNetlistViewList() -\\> str`**\n\nGets the netlist view list for the simulation options.\n\nReturns\n**out**str\nOn success, returns the netlist view list value. On failure, returns None. Check the error message by calling `lastError`.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.getNetlistViewList()\n\n`getOverwriteResult`()\n**`getOverwriteResult() -\\> bool`**\n\nGet the overwrited result.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True. Otherwise, returns False. Typical failures scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> overwritedResult = setting.getOverwriteResult()\n    >>> print(overwritedResult)\n    >>> mde.close()\n\n`getProjectDirectory`()\n**`getProjectDirectory() -\\> str`**\n\nGet the current project directory.\n\nReturns\n**out**str\nReturn a string representing the current project directory. If the `MdeSession` has been closed, an empty string is returned.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> print(\"MDE setting project directory [%s]\" % setting.getProjectDirectory())\n\n`getSettingFilePath`()\n**`getSettingFilePath() -\\> str`**\n\nGet the absolute path of the setting file.\n\nReturns\n**out**str\nReturn a string representing the setting file path. If the corresponding `MdeSession` object has been closed, an empty string will be returned.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> print(\"Setting file path [%s]\" % setting.getSettingFilePath())\n\n`getStopViewList`()\n**`getStopViewList() -\\> str`**\n\nGets the netlist stop list for the simulation options.\n\nReturns\n**out**str\nOn success, returns the stop list value. On failure, returns None. Check the error message by calling `lastError`.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.getStopViewList()\n\n`isCornerEnabled`(*name*)\n**`isCornerEnabled(name: std::string) -\\> bool`**\n\nChecks whether the corner exists and is enabled.\n\nParameters\n**name**str\nName of a corner.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nReturns true if the corner exists and is enabled. Returns false if it does not exist or is disabled.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.isCornerEnabled(\"C7\")\n\n`lastError`()\n**`lastError() -\\> str`**\n\nGets the last error message of the MdeSetting object. This last error message represents the description of the most recent error that occurs from the MdeSetting’s object instance methods. Each time an MdeSetting method is called, the previous error message is cleared.\n\nReturns\n**out**str\nReturn a string representing the last error message. If no error occurred from the last call to an MdeSetting instance method, an empty string is returned.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> sweeps = setting.getEnabledSweepList()\n    >>> if not sweeps:\n    ...     print(\"Failed to get sweep list, reason [%s]\", setting.lastError())\n\n`loadCorners`(*fileName*, *mode=2*)\n**`loadCorners(fileName: str, mode: MdeLoadCornerModeEnum=MDE_LOAD_CORNER_CANCEL) -\\> bool`**\n\nLoads corners form csv file specified by the “fileName” and “mode” parameters.\n\nParameters\n**fileName**str\nThe corner file name.\n\n**mode**MdeLoadCornerModeEnum, optional default value is MDE_LOAD_CORNER_CANCEL.\nThe mode value, default value is MDE_LOAD_CORNER_CANCEL. MdeLoadCornerModeEnum is a enumeration type, it has three modes for load corners from csv file: MDE_LOAD_CORNER_AUTO_RENAME: Rename the existing corners in mde setting and add them, and load new corner from csv into setting. MDE_LOAD_CORNER_OVERWRITE: Update the corners which already exist in mde setting, and load new corner from csv into setting. MDE_LOAD_CORNER_CANCEL: Does not add any corners, and returns False.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the csv file loaded by this method. On failure, check the error message by calling MdeSetting.lastError(). Typical failure scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed or not being in MDE L2 Spectre mode,the MdeSetting object being invalid, the “fileName” parameter having an empty value, etc.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> flag = setting.loadCorners(\"corners.csv\")\n\n`loadOutputs`(*fileName*, *mode=0*)\n**`loadOutputs(fileName: str, mode: MdeLoadOutputModeEnum=MDE_LOAD_OUTPUT_RETAIN) -\\> bool`**\n\nLoads outputs form csv file specified by the “fileName” and “mode” parameters.\n\nParameters\n**fileName**str\nThe output file name.\n\n**mode**MdeLoadOutputModeEnum\nThe mode value, default value is MDE_LOAD_OUTPUT_RETAIN. MdeLoadOutputModeEnum is an enumeration type, it has three modes for load output from csv file: MDE_LOAD_OUTPUT_RETAIN: Retain the outputs which already exist in mde setting, and load new output from csv into setting. MDE_LOAD_OUTPUT_MERGE: Update the outputs which already exist in mde setting, and load new output from csv into setting. MDE_LOAD_OUTPUT_OVERWRITE: Clear all outputs in mde setting, and load new output from csv into setting.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the csv file loaded by this method. On failure, check the error message by calling MdeSetting.lastError(). Typical failure scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed or not being in MDE L2 Spectre mode,the MdeSetting object being invalid, the “fileName” parameter having an empty value, etc.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> flag = setting.loadOutputs(\"test_out.csv\")\n\n`loadSetting`(*settingFilePath*)\n**`loadSetting(settingFilePath: std::string) -\\> bool`**\n\nLoads the setting file from disk into the current memory.\n\nParameters\n**settingFilePath**str\nThe setting file path specified by user.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns true, indicating successful loading the setting file. On failure, check the error message by calling MdeSetting.lastError(). Typical failure scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed or the setting file not exists, etc.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> isSuccess = setting.loadSetting(\"./testLib/testCell/state/setting/\")\n    >>> if isSuccess:\n    ...     print(\"Loading the setting file successfully.\")\n    ... else:\n    ...     print(\"Loading the setting file not successfully.\")\n\n`modelFileCount`(*modelFile*)\n**`modelFileCount(modelFile: std::string) -\\> int`**\n\nReturns the count of the specified model file for Nominal Corner. If the file has duplication, this method may return a value greater than 1.\n\nParameters\n**modelFile**str\nModel file name with relative path to it.\n\nReturns\n**out**int\nCount of the specified model file.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> count = setting.modelFileCount(\"modelFileName\")\n    >>> print(count)\n\n`modelFileCountForCorners`(*modelFile*)\n**`modelFileCountForCorners(modelFile: std::string) -\\> int`**\n\nReturns the count of the specified model file for corners. If the file has duplication, this method may return a value greater than 1.\n\nParameters\n**modelFile**str\nModel file name with relative path to it.\n\nReturns\n**out**int\nCount of the specified model file.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> count = setting.modelFileCountForCorners\n    >>> print(count)\n\n`modelFileExists`(*modelFile*)\n**`modelFileExists(modelFile: std::string) -\\> bool`**\n\nChecks whether model file exists or not for Nominal Corner.\n\nParameters\n**modelFile**str\nModel file name with relative path to it.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nTrue if the model file exists. False if the model file does not exist.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> if setting.modelFileExists(\"modelFileName\"):\n    ...     print(\"modelFileName\")\n\n`modelFileExistsForCorners`(*modelFile*)\n**`modelFileExistsForCorners(modelFile: std::string) -\\> bool`**\n\nChecks whether model file exists or not for corners.\n\nParameters\n**modelFile**str\nModel file name with relative path to it.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nTrue if the model file exists. False if the model file does not exist.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> if setting.modelFileExistsForCorners(\"modelFileName\"):\n    ...     print(\"modelFileName\")\n\n`outputExists`(*name*)\n**`outputExists(name: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nChecks if an output specified by the “name” parameter already exists.\n\nParameters\n**name**str\nThe specified parameter name.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nReturns True if the output already exists. Returns False otherwise.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.addSpeOutput(MdeSpeOutput(name=\"corner_max\", expr=\"max(VT(SUB),overall=t)\",\n    ... exprType=\"Expression\", evalType=\"Corners\", save=False, plot=True))\n    >>> assert(setting.outputExists())\n    >>> setting.removeOutput(\"corner_max\")\n    >>> assert(not setting.outputExists())\n\n`removeCorner`(*name*)\n**`removeCorner(name: std::string)`**\n\nRemoves the corner with the specified name. Does nothing if the corner does not exist.\n\nParameters\n**name**str\nName of a corner.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.removeCorner(\"C4\")\n\n`removeModelFile`(*modelFile*, *duplicatesIndex=0*)\n**`removeModelFile(modelFile: std::string, duplicatesIndex: int=0)`**\n\nRemove a model file from Nominal Corner. If the specified model file has duplication, the second parameter is required to distinguish which model file row to remove.\n\nParameters\n**modelFile**str\nModel file name with relative path to it.\n\n**duplicatesIndex**int, optional\nSpecifies which of duplicates to be selected. Specify 0 if there are no duplicates or first duplicate is needed. This value is the default and could be omitted.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.removeModelFile(\"modelFileName\", 1)\n\n`removeModelFileForCorners`(*modelFile*, *duplicatesIndex=0*)\n**`removeModelFileForCorners(modelFile: std::string, duplicatesIndex: int=0)`**\n\nRemove a model file from corner setup. If the specified model file has duplication, the second parameter is required to distinguish which model file row to remove.\n\nParameters\n**modelFile**str\nModel file name with relative path to it.\n\n**duplicatesIndex**int, optional\nSpecifies which of duplicates to be selected. Specify 0 if there are no duplicates or first duplicate is needed. This value is the default and could be omitted.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.removeModelFileForCorners(\"modelFileName\", 1)\n\n`removeOutput`(*name*)\n**`removeOutput(name: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nRemove an output specified by the output name.\n\nParameters\n**name**str\nThe specified output name.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nIf the output exists, the method will remove it and returns True. If the output does not exist or the corresponding MdeSession has been closed, it will return False. On failure, check the error message by calling `lastError`.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.addSpeOutput(MdeSpeOutput(name=\"corner_max\", expr=\"max(VT(SUB),overall=t)\",\n    ... exprType=\"Expression\", evalType=\"Corners\", save=False, plot=True))\n    >>> setting.removeOutput(\"corner_max\")\n\n`removeParameter`(*paramName*)\n**`removeParameter(paramName: std::string)`**\n\nRemove a parameter for Nominal Corner. If the parameter has not been added, nothing will happen.\n\nParameters\n**paramName**str\nParameter name to be removed.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.removeParameter(\"parameterName\")\n\n`removeParameterForCorners`(*paramName*)\n**`removeParameterForCorners(paramName: std::string)`**\n\nRemove a parameter for corners. If the parameter has not been added, nothing will happen.\n\nParameters\n**paramName**str\nParameter name to be removed.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.removeParameterForCorners(\"parameterName\")\n\n`saveCornersToDir`(*path*)\n**`saveCornersToDir(path: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSave the corners of the MdeSetting object into the directory specified by the “path” parameter.A csv file will be created in that directory.\n\nParameters\n**path**str\nThe path to save corner file.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the csv file created by this method. On failure, check the error message by calling MdeSetting.lastError(). Typical failure scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed or not being in MDE L2 Spectre mode, the MdeSetting object being invalid, no permission to create the directory specified by the parameter “path”, etc.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> flag = setting.saveCornersToDir(\"test_save_corner\")\n\n`saveOutputsToDir`(*path*)\n**`saveOutputsToDir(path: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSave the outputs of the MdeSetting object into the directory specified by the “path” parameter. A csv file will be created in that directory.\n\nParameters\n**path**str\nThe outputs file path.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns true, representing the csv file created by this method. On failure, check the error message by calling MdeSetting.lastError(). Typical failure scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed or not being in MDE L2 Spectre mode,the MdeSetting object being invalid, no permission to create the directory specified by the parameter “path”, etc.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> corners = setting.getAllSpeCorners()\n\n`saveSetting`(*destDir*)\n**`saveSetting(destDir: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSave the information in the MdeSetting object into a “setting” file in the directory specified by parameter “destDir”. The original setting file from which the current `MdeSession` is created can be overwritten through this way.\n\nParameters\n**destDir**str\nThe target directory.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True. Otherwise, returns False. Typical failure scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed, the directory specified by parameter “destDir” cannot be created, etc.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.addSpeOutput(MdeSpeOutput(name=\"corner_max\", expr=\"max(VT(SUB),overall=t)\",\n    ... exprType=\"Expression\", evalType=\"Corners\", save=False, plot=True))\n    >>> setting.saveSetting(\"testLib/testCell/state_new\")\n\n`setAcAnalysis`(*analysis*)\n**`setAcAnalysis(analysis: MdeAcAnalysis) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets ac analysis by the given MdeAcAnalysis object. After setting the Ac analysis, it needs to be enabled by calling enableAcAnalysis.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that the specified ac analysis has been added to the MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> ac = ae.MdeAcAnalysis()\n    >>> sweepVar = ae.MdeSweepVariable()\n    >>> sweepVar.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_VARIABLE_MODEL_PARAMETER\n    >>> sweepVar.modelName = \"C0\"\n    >>> sweepVar.modelParameterName = \"I0\"\n    >>> sweepVar.freForMod = \"10\"\n    >>> ac.setSweepVariable(sweepVar)\n    >>> sr = ae.MdeSweepRange()\n    >>> sr.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_RANGE_CENTER_SPAN\n    >>> sr.center = \"10\"\n    >>> sr.span = \"10\"\n    >>> ac.setSweepRange(sr)\n    >>> st = ae.MdeSweepType()\n    >>> st.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_TYPE_LOG\n    >>> st.logMode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_TYPE_LOG_NUM_STEP\n    >>> st.numberOfStepsForLog = \"10\"\n    >>> ac.setSweepType(st)\n    >>> sp = ae.MdeAddSpecificPoints()\n    >>> sp.addSpecificPointsStatue = True\n    >>> sp.specificPoints = \"I0 I1\"\n    >>> ac.setAddSpecificPoints(sp)\n    >>> setting.setAcAnalysis(ac)\n\n`setCustom`(*key*, *val*)\n**`setCustom(key: str, val: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets custom key value pair in mde setting. To save the custom key to the setting file, use command MdeSetting::saveSetting or click Session-\\>save State in MDE window.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.attachToGui(pyScript.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setCustom(\"keyword\", \"value\")\n\n`setCustomDigitalSolver`(*customSlover*)\n**`setCustomDigitalSolver(customSlover: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets custom digital solver.\n\nParameters\n**customSlover**str\nCustom digital solver. The default value is “”.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the digital solver has been set successfully.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setCustomDigitalSolver(\"mysolver\")\n\n`setDcAnalysis`(*analysis*)\n**`setDcAnalysis(analysis: MdeDcAnalysis) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets dc analysis by the given MdeDcAnalysis object. After setting the dc analysis, it needs to be enabled by calling enableDcAnalysis.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that the specified dc analysis has been added to the MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> dc = ae.MdeDcAnalysis()\n    >>> dc.setSaveDcOperatingPointStatus(False)\n    >>> dc.setHysteresisSweep(True)\n    >>> sweepVar = ae.MdeSweepVariable()\n    >>> sweepVar.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_VARIABLE_MODEL_PARAMETER\n    >>> sweepVar.modelName = \"C0\"\n    >>> sweepVar.modelParameterName = \"I0\"\n    >>> dc.setSweepVariable(sweepVar)\n    >>> sr = ae.MdeSweepRange()\n    >>> sr.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_RANGE_CENTER_SPAN\n    >>> sr.center = \"10\"\n    >>> sr.span = \"10\"\n    >>> dc.setSweepRange(sr)\n    >>> st = ae.MdeSweepType()\n    >>> st.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_TYPE_LOG\n    >>> st.logMode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_TYPE_LOG_NUM_STEP\n    >>> st.numberOfStepsForLog = \"10\"\n    >>> dc.setSweepType(st)\n    >>> sp = ae.MdeAddSpecificPoints()\n    >>> sp.addSpecificPointsStatue = True\n    >>> sp.specificPoints = \"I0 I1\"\n    >>> dc.setAddSpecificPoints(sp)\n    >>> setting.setDcAnalysis(dc)\n    >>> setting.enableDcAnalysis()\n\n`setDesign`(*libName*, *cellName*, *viewName*)\n**`setDesign(libName: str, cellName: str, viewName: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets the lib, cell and view which are specified by user for the design.\n\nParameters\n**libName: str**\nSets the libname of the new design.\n\n**cellName: str**\nSets the cellname of the new design.\n\n**viewName: str**\nSets the viewname of the new design.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the new design has been set successfully.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setDesign(\"lib\", \"cell\", \"schematic\")\n\n`setDigitalFormat`(*format=0*)\n**`setDigitalFormat(format: MdeAlpsCSDigitalFormatEnum) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets digital solver format.\n\nParameters\n**format**MdeAlpsCSDigitalFormatEnum\nThe format value, default value is MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_FORMAT_VCD. MdeAlpsCSDigitalFormatEnum is an enumeration type, it has two format for AlpsCS supports. MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_FORMAT_VCD means set digital with VCD format. MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_FORMAT_FSDB means set digital with FSDB format.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the digital solver format has been set successfully. On failure, check the error message by calling MdeSetting.lastError(). Typical failure scenarios include setting the wrong format.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setDigitalFormat(pyScript.MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_FORMAT_VCD)\n\n`setDigitalSolver`(*mode=0*)\n**`setDigitalSolver(mode: MdeAlpsCSDigitalSolverEnum) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets digital solver type.\n\nParameters\n**mode**MdeAlpsCSDigitalSolverEnum\nThe mode value, default value is MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_MS. MdeAlpsCSDigitalSolverEnum is an enumeration type, it has five modes for AlpsCS supports. MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_MS : Support for MS digital solver. MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_NC : Support for NC digital solver. MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_VCS : Support for VCS digital solver. MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_UVS : Support for UVS digital solver. MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_CUSTOM : Support for Custom digital solver.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the digital solver has been set successfully. On failure, check the error message by calling MdeSetting.lastError(). Typical failure scenarios include setting the wrong digital solver type.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setDigitalSolver(pyScript.MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_MS)\n\n`setDigitalSolverArgs`(*args*)\n**`setDigitalSolverArgs(arguments: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets digital solver arguments.\n\nParameters\n**arguments: str**\nSets digital solver arguments. The default value is “”.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the digital solver arguments has been set successfully.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setDigitalSolverArgs(\"-args name\")\n\n`setJobPolicy`(*jobPolicy*)\n**`setJobPolicy(jobPolicy: MdeJobPolicy) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets job policy specified by “jobPolicy” parameter. MdeJobPolicy is a base class, and it has four sub-class: `MdeLocalJobPolicy`: Sets local job policy. `MdeLSFJobPolicy`: Sets lsf job policy. `MdeOGEJobPolicy`: Sets oge job policy. `MdeDonauJobPolicy`: Sets donau job policy.\n\nParameters\n**jobPolicy**MdeJobPolicy\nThe job policy\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing job policy set by this method. On failure, check the error message by calling MdeSetting.lastError(). Typical failure scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed or not being in MDE L2 Spectre mode,the MdeSetting object being invalid, etc.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> # Add local job\n    >>> local = pyScript.MdeLocalJobPolicy()\n    >>> local.setMaxJobNum(6)\n    >>> flag = setting.setJobPolicy(local)\n    >>> # Add lsf job\n    >>> lsf = pyScript.MdeLSFJobPolicy(\"test_lsf_job\", \"priority\", , 2)\n    >>> flag = setting.setJobPolicy(lsf)\n    >>> # Add OGE job\n    >>> oge = pyScript.MdeOGEJobPolicy(\"test_oge_job\", \"all.q\", , 3)\n    >>> flag = setting.setJobPolicy(oge)\n\n`setNetlistMaxErrorsNum`(*maxErrsNum*)\n**`setNetlistMaxErrorsNum(maxErrsNum: unsigned) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets maximum error message number to be reported by netlister.\n\nParameters\n**maxErrsNum**unsigned integer\nMaximum number of error messages to be set.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nTrue if successful set, false otherwise.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setNetlistMaxErrorsNum(10)\n    >>> files = mde.createDesignNetlist(\"./netlistDir\")\n\n`setNetlistViewList`(*viewList*)\n**`setNetlistViewList(viewList: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets the netlist view list for the simulation options.\n\nParameters\n**viewList: str**\nThe new netlist view list.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the new netlist view list has been set successfully.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setNetlistViewList(\"spectreText spectre schematic veriloga\")\n\n`setNoiseAnalysis`(*analysis*)\n**`setNoiseAnalysis(analysis: MdeNoiseAnalysis) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets noise analysis by the given MdeNoiseAnalysis object. After setting the noise analysis, it needs to be enabled by calling enableNoiseAnalysis.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that the specified noise analysis has been added to the MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> noise = ae.MdeNoiseAnalysis()\n    >>> sweepVar = ae.MdeSweepVariable()\n    >>> sweepVar.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_VARIABLE_MODEL_PARAMETER\n    >>> sweepVar.modelName = \"C0\"\n    >>> sweepVar.modelParameterName = \"I0\"\n    >>> sweepVar.freForMod = \"10\"\n    >>> noise.setSweepVariable(sweepVar)\n    >>> sr = ae.MdeSweepRange()\n    >>> sr.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_RANGE_CENTER_SPAN\n    >>> sr.center = \"10\"\n    >>> sr.span = \"10\"\n    >>> noise.setSweepRange(sr)\n    >>> st = ae.MdeSweepType()\n    >>> st.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_TYPE_LOG\n    >>> st.logMode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_TYPE_LOG_NUM_STEP\n    >>> st.numberOfStepsForLog = \"10\"\n    >>> noise.setSweepType(st)\n    >>> sp = ae.MdeAddSpecificPoints()\n    >>> sp.addSpecificPointsStatue = True\n    >>> sp.specificPoints = \"I0 I1\"\n    >>> noise.setAddSpecificPoints(sp)\n    >>> noise.setOutputNoiseMode(ae.MDE_OUTPUT_NOISE_PROBE)\n    >>> noise.setOutputProbeInstance(\"aaa\")\n    >>> noise.setInputNoiseMode(ae.MDE_INPUT_NOISE_VOLTAGE)\n    >>> noise.setInputVoltageSrc(\"777\")\n    >>> noise.setNoiseSeparationStatus(True)\n    >>> setting.setNoiseAnalysis(noise)\n\n`setOverwriteResult`(*resultName*)\n**`setOverwriteResult(resultName: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSet the overwrited result.\n\nParameters\n**resultName**str\nThe name of the overwrited result.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True. Otherwise, returns False. Typical failures scenarios include the corresponding MdeSession object having been closed, the result name is empty or the result not existing.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> isSucc = setting.setOverwriteResult(\"Result1\")\n    >>> if isSucc:\n    ...     print(\"Sets the overwrited result succeeds\")\n    ... else:\n    ...     print(\"Sets the overwrited result failed\")\n    >>> mde.close()\n\n`setProjectDirectory`(*path*)\n**`setProjectDirectory(path: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets the project directory. Further calls to `MdeSession.netlistAndRun` and `MdeSession.createSimulationNetlist` method will create their result data into the new project directory.\n\nParameters\n**path**str\nThe project directory.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nReturns True on success. Otherwise, returns False. On failure, check the error message by calling `lastError`. A typical failure scenario is calling it after the MdeSession object is closed,\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"testLib\", \"testCell\", \"state\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setProjectDirectory(\"./simProjectDir\")\n\n`setStbAnalysis`(*analysis*)\n**`setStbAnalysis(analysis: MdeStbAnalysis) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets stb analysis by the given MdeStbAnalysis object. After setting the stb analysis, it needs to be enabled by calling enableStbAnalysis.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, return True, indicating that the specified stb analysis has been added to the MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> stb = ae.MdeStbAnalysis()\n    >>> sweepVar = ae.MdeSweepVariable()\n    >>> sweepVar.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_VARIABLE_MODEL_PARAMETER\n    >>> sweepVar.modelName = \"C0\"\n    >>> sweepVar.modelParameterName = \"I0\"\n    >>> sweepVar.freForMod = \"10\"\n    >>> stb.setSweepVariable(sweepVar)\n    >>> sr = ae.MdeSweepRange()\n    >>> sr.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_RANGE_CENTER_SPAN\n    >>> sr.center = \"10\"\n    >>> sr.span = \"10\"\n    >>> stb.setSweepRange(sr)\n    >>> st = ae.MdeSweepType()\n    >>> st.mode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_TYPE_LOG\n    >>> st.logMode = ae.MDE_SWEEP_TYPE_LOG_NUM_STEP\n    >>> st.numberOfStepsForLog = \"10\"\n    >>> stb.setSweepType(st)\n    >>> sp = ae.MdeAddSpecificPoints()\n    >>> sp.addSpecificPointsStatue = True\n    >>> sp.specificPoints = \"I0 I1\"\n    >>> stb.setAddSpecificPoints(sp)\n    >>> stb.setProbeInst(\"aaa\")\n    >>> stb.setModeTypeStatus(True)\n    >>> setting.setStbAnalysis(stb)\n\n`setStopViewList`(*stopList*)\n**`setStopViewList(stopList: str) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets the netlist stop list for the simulation options.\n\nParameters\n**stopList: str**\nThe new netlist stop list.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the new netlist stop list has been set successfully.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setStopViewList(\"spectreText spectre\")\n\n`setTranAnalysis`(*analysis*)\n**`setTranAnalysis(analysis: MdeTranAnalysis) -\\> bool`**\n\nSets tran analysis by the given MdeTranAnalysis object. After setting the tran analysis, it needs to be enabled by calling enableTranAnalysis.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, indicating that the specified tran analysis has been added to the MDE setting. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as ae\n    >>> mde = ae.MdeSession_attachToGui(ae.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> tran = ae.MdeTranAnalysis()\n    >>> tran.setStop(\"200n\")\n    >>> tran.setAccuracyLevel(ae.MDE_TRAN_ACC_LEVEL_CONSERVATIVE)\n    >>> tran.setTransientNoiseStatus(True)\n    >>> tran.setNoiseFmax(\"2\")\n    >>> tran.setNoiseFmin(\"2\")\n    >>> tran.setNoiseSeed(\"2\")\n    >>> tran.setNoiseTmin(\"2\")\n    >>> tran.setNoiseUpdate(ae.MDE_TRAN_NOISE_UPDATE_FMAX)\n    >>> tran.setMultipleRunsStatus(True)\n    >>> tran.setNumberOfRuns(\"200\")\n    >>> tran.setNoiseContribution(ae.MDE_TRAN_NOISE_CONTRIBUTION_ON)\n    >>> tran.setInstanceList(\"I0 I1\")\n    >>> tran.setNoiseSeed(\"21\")\n    >>> tran.setNoiseScale(\"11\")\n    >>> setting.setTranAnalysis(tran)\n    >>> setting.enableTranAnalysis()\n\n`turnOff64Bit`()\n**`turnOff64Bit() -\\> bool`**\n\nSets NC or VCS digital solver is not in 64-bit mode.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the nc or vcs solver has been set successfully not in 64-bit mode.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setCustomDigitalSolver(\"pyScript.MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_NC\")\n    >>> setting.turnOff64Bit()\n\n`turnOn64Bit`()\n**`turnOn64Bit() -\\> bool`**\n\nSets NC or VCS digital solver in 64-bit mode.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns True, representing the nc or vcs solver has been set successfully in 64-bit mode.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.open(\"test\", \"test\", \"mde\")\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.setCustomDigitalSolver(\"pyScript.MDE_ALPS_CS_DIGITAL_SOLVER_NC\")\n    >>> setting.turnOn64Bit()\n\n`updateSettingFromGui`()\n**`updateSettingFromGui() -\\> bool`**\n\nSync all contents in the GUI to the settings.\n\nReturns\n**out**bool\nOn success, returns true, all contents in the GUI will sync to the settings. Otherwise, returns False.\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> mde = pyScript.MdeSession.attachToGui(pyScript.mdeGetLastActiveWindowId())\n    >>> setting = mde.getSetting()\n    >>> setting.updateSettingFromGui()",
