  "api_descriptions": "# emyNet\n\n*class* `emyNet`(*\\*args*, *\\*\\*kwargs*)\n\n- lowest numbered bit of all of the associated busNets\n\n- highest numbered bit of all of the associated busNets\n\n- busNets with the same base name\n\n- associated busNetBits\n\nIf each bit of the busNetBits does not exist, the bus network bit is automatically created. They can be used for applications that perform scaled connectivity traversal of data.\n\nThe bundle network may comprise a scalar network or a bus. When creating `emyBundleNet`, in addition to the bundle net itself, scalar net and bus net will also be created automatically.\n\nAll automatically created network objects are considered “implicit”. The network iterator can use the filter flag so as not to access the implicit network during traversal. Implicit networks are more limited in the operations that allow them to be used. Implicit networks cannot be explicitly destroyed by users. Some properties can only be set on explicit network objects – for example, parasitic confidence. When the caller explicitly creates a network with the same name, the implicit network can be explicitly created.\n\nThe name is usually associated with the network. Various network objects obtain and return names through the common `emyName` object, but also use `emyScalarName`, `emyVectorBitName`, `emyVectorName` and `emyBundleName` objects. These name objects manage the mapping of names from one namespace to another. For example, a net is created using the name in CDBA nameSpace; another application can retrieve the net’s name in the Verilog nameSpace.\n\nThere may be two or more equivalent networks. The equivalent network traverses independently or logically as the same network. Only single bit networks can be set to be equivalent to each other.\n\nYou can associate geometric `emyConnFig` objects with networks: shapes, routes, and guides. A network is required to create other connection objects, such as the `emyTerm` object.\n\n*static* `create`(*block*, *name*, *sigType=0*, *isGlobal=False*, *view=0*)\n**`create(block: emyBlock, name: emyName, sigType: emySigType = emcSignalSigType, isGlobal: emyBoolean = False, view: emyBlockDomainVisibility = emcInheritFromTopBlock) -\\> emyNet`**\n\nCreates a network in the specified *design* with the specified name. The type of network created (`emyScalarNet`, `emyBusNetBit`, `emyBusNet`, or `emyBundleNet`) is determined by the specified name. If the specified name is hierarchical, and the hierarchical part of the path exists, and there is no `emyOccNet` with the specified name, the network is created in the event specified by the path.\n\nParameters\n**block :**\nThe block in which to create the net\n\n**name :**\nThe net name\n\n**sigType :**\nThe signal type to associate with the net; if not specified, the default is emcSignalSigType\n\n**isGlobal :**\nSpecifies if this net is considered global; if not specified, the default is False.\n\n**view :**\nSpecifies whether this net is visible in the module domain\n\nReturns\nReturns the emyNet\n\nRaises\nemcBusNetBaseNameMatchesScalarName :\n\nemcBusNetNameMatchesAutoName :\n\nemcInvalidNetName :\n\nemcNetExists :\n\nemcScalarNetNameMatchesBusBaseName :\n\nemcHierPathDoesNotExist :\n\nemcHierPathCrossDesign :\n\n`destroy`()\n**`destroy()`**\n\nDestroys this net, removing it from the database.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotDestroyImplicitNet :\n\nemcCannotDestroyNetInNonUniqueSpan :\n\nemcCannotDestroyNetOnHiddenTerm :\n\n*static* `find`(*block*, *name*)\n**`find(block: emyBlock, name: emyName) -\\> emyNet`**\n\nSearches the specified block for a network with the specified name. If found, the function returns the network. Otherwise, null is returned. The path part of the name must specify the path of an existing reference in the design. The hierarchy name is regarded as an alias that identifies emyOccNet in the appearance domain. If the specified name is hierarchical, the return value is the canonical network in the block domain of the specified alias.\n\nParameters\n**block :**\nThe block to search\n\n**name :**\nThe net name to match\n\n`getBit`(*bitIndex*)\n**`getBit(bitIndex: emyUInt4) -\\> emyBitNet`**\n\nReturns the net, which corresponds to the specified *bitindex* bit of the network. For scalarnet, this function only returns the network. For bus network, return the bus bit corresponding to *bitindex* . For example, if this net is a busNet “a\\[7:0\\]” and\\*bitIndex\\*is zero, return the busNetBit corresponding to “a\\[7\\]”. For bundleNets, a scalarNet or busNetBit is returned.\n\nParameters\n**bitIndex :**\nSpecifies which bit of the net to return\n\nReturns\nReturns an emyNet\n\nRaises\nemcInvalidBusNetBitIndex :\n\nemcInvalidNetIndex :\n\n`getDefaultConstraintGroup`()\n**`getDefaultConstraintGroup() -\\> emyConstraintGroup`**\n\nReturn the constraint group of this emyNet. The constraints in this constraint group apply to all objects that make up emyNet, such as shapes, alignments, pins, and terminals. If there is no constraint on the network, a new group is created.\n\n`getGuides`(*includeRouteGuides=True*)\n**`getGuides(includeRouteGuides: emyBoolean = True) -\\> emyCollection_emyGuide_emyNet`**\n\nReturns the collection of guides associated with this network. The optional Boolean parameter ‘includeRouteGuides’ allows the application to customize the guide collection by including or excluding guides that are part of the route on this network. The default behavior is to return all guidelines that may be explicit or implicit on this net.\n\nParameters\n**includeRouteGuides :**\nAllows application to include or exclude the guides that may be part of routes on this net\n\n`getInstTerms`(*filterFlags=2*)\n**`getInstTerms(filterFlags: emyUInt4 = emcInstTermIterNotImplicit) -\\> emyCollection_emyInstTerm_emyNet`**\n\nReturns the instTerms collection in this network. The filter flag bit is defined as follows, and can be logically OR’d operated to optimize the contents of the collection.\n\nParameters\n**filterFlags :**\nSpecifies what the collection contains. The bits flags are defined as follows:\n\n- *emcInstTermIterNotImplicit:* the collection will only contain instTerms that were explicitly created\n\n- *emcInstTermIterEquivNets:* the collection will also contain the instTerms on the nets that are equivalent to this one\n\nRaises\nemcInstTermIterFlagNotApplicableOnNets :\n\n`getMemberNets`(*unique=True*)\n**`getMemberNets(unique: emyBoolean = True) -\\> emyMemNetCollection`**\n\nThe collection whose members are net will be returned. For example, if a design contains scalar net a and bundle net x ,y, a, then this collection for net a contains both nets a and x ,y, a.\n\nIn particular:\n\n- Explicit nets are always members of themselves so the collection is never empty for such nets.\n\n- Implicit nets are never returned in this collection.\n\n- BundleNets can only be members of themselves.\n\n- ScalarNets and busNets are members of themselves and bundleNets.\n\n- BusNetBits are members of all busNets where the bit is present so busNetBit`A\\[1\\]`is a member of`A\\[2:0\\]`\n\n- A single-bit busNet will only return itself\n\n- Nets are members of bundles that contain a member that is in exactly the same form as the specified net\n\n- A\\[1:0\\]`is \\*not\\* a member of`A\\[4:0\\]\n\n- A\\[1:0\\]`is \\*not\\* a member of`A\\[0:1\\]\n\n- Where a net occurs multiple times in a bundle, it will occur multiple times in this collection. See `emyMemNetIter` for details about iterating over this collection.\n\nParameters\n**unique :**\nSpecifies that only the preferred equivalent nets are included in the collection\n\n`getName`(*\\*args*)\n**`getName(name: emyName)`**\n\n**`getName(ns: emyNameSpace, name: emyString)`**\n\nHint\n\nThis is an overloaded function. See below for more details.\n\n- **`getName(name: emyName)`**\n\n  > The name of this net in the *name* argument will be returned.\n\n- **`getName(ns: emyNameSpace, name: emyString)`**\n\n  > Returns the name of this net in the specified nameSpace in the specified *name* string.\n\n`getNumBits`()\n**`getNumBits() -\\> emyUInt4`**\n\nReturns the number of bits in this net.\n\n`getPins`()\n**`getPins() -\\> emyCollection_emyPin_emyNet`**\n\nThe collection of pins on this net will be returned.\n\n`getPriority`()\n**`getPriority() -\\> emyInt4`**\n\nReturned The priority value of this net. If a priority has never been set, this function will returns 0.\n\n`getRoutes`()\n**`getRoutes() -\\> emyCollection_emyRoute_emyNet`**\n\nThe collection of routes in this net will be returned.\n\n`getShapes`(*filterFlags=1*)\n**`getShapes(filterFlags: emyUInt4 = emcShapeIterNetRoutes) -\\> emyCollection_emyShape_emyNet`**\n\nReturns the collection of shapes on this network. An application can customize a set of shapes on the network to include shapes (pathSegs) that are part of routes on the same network, or to implement the shapes of pins on all terminals on the network. By default, alignments on the same network contain shapes. The collection always contains shapes that are explicitly located on the net.\n\nThe filter flags can be specified as bitwise or a combination of the following: emcShapeIterNetOnly, emcShapeIterNetRoutes or emcShapeIterNetPins. emcShapeIterNetOnly can only be used alone when an explicit set of shapes on the network is required. This means that emcShapeIterNetRoutes and emcShapeIterNetPins can be used together and return the shape in the route on the network or the shape of the implementation pin on the network terminal. Note that the collection will never include shapes contained in vias associated with networks or network routes, nor will it include shapes contained in vias or instances associated with network pins.\n\nParameters\n**filterFlags :**\nThis value specifies the customization required by an application\n\n`getSigType`()\n**`getSigType() -\\> emySigType`**\n\nThe signal type of this net will be returned.\n\n`getSingleBitMembers`()\n**`getSingleBitMembers() -\\> emyCollection_emyBitNet_emyNet`**\n\nReturns a group of company member networks in this network. If this network is a unit network, the collection contains itself. If this network is a busNet, the collection contains all the corresponding busNetBits.\n\n`getSource`()\n**`getSource() -\\> emySource`**\n\nreturned The source value of this net.\n\n`getSteiners`()\n**`getSteiners() -\\> emyCollection_emySteiner_emyNet`**\n\nThe collection of Steiners associated with this net will be returned.\n\n`getTerms`(*filterflags=16*)\n**`getTerms(filterflags: emyUInt4 = emcTermIterNotImplicit) -\\> emyCollection_emyTerm_emyNet`**\n\nReturns the terminal collection in this modNet. By default, the collection contains only explicit terminals associated with this network. When emcTermIterAll is included in *filterFlags*, the set will contain all terminals associated with this network, including implicit terminals.\n\n- When emcTermIterEquivNets is included in *filterFlags* , the collection will contain all terminals in the set of nets that are equivalent to this net.\n\nParameters\n**filterFlags :**\nSpecifies which types of terminals to include in the collection\n\nReturns\n**out**emyCollection_emyTerm_emyNet\n\nExamples\n\n    >>> import pyAether as pyScript\n    >>> cv = pyScript.dbOpenCV(\"test\", \"test\")\n    >>> net = pyScript.dbCrtNet(cv, \"net\")\n    >>> term = pyScript.dbCrtTerm(net, \"term\", \"input\")\n    >>> res = net.getTerms()\n    res = [Term (Name: term)]\n\n`getVias`(*filterFlags=1*)\n**`getVias(filterFlags: emyUInt4 = emcViaIterNetRoutes) -\\> emyCollection_emyVia_emyNet`**\n\nThe collection of vias associated with this net will be returned.\n\nParameters\n**filterFlags :**\n\n**filterFlags :**\nSpecifies what the collection contains. The bits flags are defined as follows:\n\n- *emcViaIterNetOnly:* the collection will only all vias associated with this net\n\n- *emcViaIterNetRoutes:* the collection will only contain vias that are associated with routes\n\n- *emcViaIterNetPins:* the collection will only contain the vias that are associated with pins\n\n`hasDefaultConstraintGroup`()\n**`hasDefaultConstraintGroup() -\\> emyBoolean`**\n\nTrue will be returned if there are constraints associated with this net.\n\n`isEmpty`()\n**`isEmpty() -\\> emyBoolean`**\n\nReturns True if this net has any objects attached to it or associated with it.\n\n`isGlobal`()\n**`isGlobal() -\\> emyBoolean`**\n\nReturns a boolean value that indicates if this net is a global net.\n\n`isImplicit`()\n**`isImplicit() -\\> emyBoolean`**\n\nReturns a Boolean value indicating whether this network is implicit, which is automatically created when creating bundleNet or busNet.\n\n*static* `isValidName`(*block*, *name*)\n**`isValidName(block: emyBlock, name: emyName) -\\> emyBoolean`**\n\nThe function is to check whether the specified name is valid for the new emyNet in the specified block. False if the network name is hierarchical and found in the presence domain. If the name of the network is hierarchical, but the specified pathname does not appear, False is returned.\n\n`merge`(*fromNet*)\n**`merge(fromNet: emyNet)`**\n\nMerges the specified *fromNet* into this network. Both networks must have the same number of *bits* All the following objects in *fromNet* are transferred to this network: terminal, terminology, graphics, guidelines, properties and textDisplays.\n\nThe network attributes are merged to keep the higher network priority between the two networks. If *fromNet* is global, the network is global.\n\nIf both nets have properties of the same name, the properties on this net are retained.\n\nIf the *fromNet* is equivalent to other nets, those nets are also made equivalent to this net. If the nets are multi-bit nets, equivalences between scalar members are established for those members that are not implicit. For example, if there are nets “x,y”, “a,b”, “x”, “y”, “a”, and “b” and “a,b” is merged into “x,y”, net “a” is made equivalent to “x” and net “b” is made equivalent to “y.”\n\nThe *fromNet* is then destroyed.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotMergeToImplicitNet :\n\nemcCannotMergeNetsWithDiffNumBits :\n\nemcMergeNetsNotInSameBlock :\n\nemcCannotEditNetOnHiddenTerm :\n\nemcMergeNetsMustBeInUniqueOccHier :\n\nemcTermMustJoinSameNet :\n\n`scalarize`()\n**`scalarize()`**\n\nEnsures that the bitnets associated with this network have been upgraded to an explicit state so that they can support implementation data such as shapes and routes.\n\nIf the network is a multi bit network, this function ensures that all constituent bit networks are promoted to an explicit state. The multi bit network is then degraded to an implicit state so that no data is associated with it. When the network is degraded to an implicit state, the associated implementation data will be deleted from it.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotScalarizeImplicitNet :\n\n`setGlobal`(*isGlobal*)\n**`setGlobal(isGlobal: emyBoolean)`**\n\nSets the global properties of this block net. Note that when the block network is set to global, the network will be merged into the global network. The object representing the global block network may be different from the object in the original non global block net.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotSetGlobalOnImplicitNet :\n\n`setPriority`(*priority*)\n**`setPriority(priority: emyInt4)`**\n\nThe priority value will be set to this net. The specified *priority* value must be in the range of -128 to 128. The default priority is 0 if no set has been done.\n\nRaises\nemcInvalidNetPriority :\n\nemcCannotSetPriorityOnImplicitNet :\n\n`setSigType`(*sigType*)\n**`setSigType(sigType: emySigType)`**\n\nThe sigType attribute of this net will be set to the specified value.\n\nNote: The sigType of an emyNet can be different from the sigType of its corresponding `emyModNet` . In other words, this function sets the sigType on this net in the block domain only.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotSetSigTypeOnImplicitNet :\n\nemcInvalidSigTypeForBlockOverrideNet :\n\n`setSource`(*source*)\n**`setSource(source: emySource)`**\n\nThe source for this net will be set to the specified value.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotSetSourceOnImplicitNet :\n\n`transfer`(*fromNet*)\n**`transfer(fromNet: emyNet)`**\n\nTransfer objects from the specified *fromNet* to this network. Shapes, alignments, terminals, and instance terminals are moved from the specified network to this network. Copy or merge attributes and update the text display accordingly.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotTransferToImplicitNet :\n\nemcCannotTransferNetWithInstTerm :\n\nemcCannotTransferNetWithTerm :\n\nemcTransferNetsNotInSameBlock :\n\nemcTransferNetsMustBeInUniqueOccHier :\n\n---\n\n## 补充说明（通过测试验证）\n\n# emyNet API 测试经验总结\n\n## 概述\n`emyNet` 类是 pyAether 中用于表示设计网络中网络对象的核心类。它支持标量网络、总线网络和束网络，提供了丰富的网络操作功能。\n\n## API 功能分析\n\n### 1. 网络创建\n- **主要创建方法**: `emyNet.create(block, name, sigType, isGlobal, view)`\n- **简化创建方法**: `dbCrtNet(cv, name)` - 更简单易用\n- **网络类型**: 根据名称自动识别创建标量网络、总线网络或束网络\n\n### 2. 基本属性操作\n- **优先级管理**: `setPriority()`, `getPriority()` - 优先级范围 -128 到 128\n- **全局网络设置**: `setGlobal()`, `isGlobal()` - 可将网络设置为全局网络\n- **信号类型**: `setSigType()`, `getSigType()` - 需要正确的 `emySigType` 参数\n- **隐式网络**: `isImplicit()` - 标识网络是否为隐式创建\n\n### 3. 网络查询\n- **查找网络**: `emyNet.find(block, name)` - 需要 `emyBlock` 对象\n- **名称验证**: `emyNet.isValidName(block, name)` - 检查名称是否有效\n- **位操作**: `getBit(bitIndex)` - 获取网络的指定位\n- **成员网络**: `getMemberNets()`, `getSingleBitMembers()` - 获取相关网络\n\n### 4. 集合操作\n- **终端集合**: `getTerms()`, `getInstTerms()` - 获取网络上的终端\n- **引脚集合**: `getPins()` - 获取网络上的引脚\n- **布线集合**: `getRoutes()`, `getShapes()`, `getVias()`, `getGuides()`, `getSteiners()`\n- **约束组**: `getDefaultConstraintGroup()`, `hasDefaultConstraintGroup()`\n\n### 5. 高级操作\n- **网络合并**: `merge(fromNet)` - 合并两个网络\n- **网络转移**: `transfer(fromNet)` - 转移网络对象\n- **标量化**: `scalarize()` - 将多比特网络转换为显式状态\n- **网络销毁**: `destroy()` - 销毁网络对象\n\n## 参数使用技巧\n\n### 1. 网络名称创建\n```python\n# 正确方式：使用 emyNativeNS 创建 emyName\nnative_ns = pa.emyNativeNS()\nnet_name = pa.emyName(native_ns, \"net_name\")\n\n# 简化方式：使用 emyString 配合 dbCrtNet\nnet_name_str = pa.emyString(\"net_name\")\nnet = pa.dbCrtNet(cv, net_name_str)\n```\n\n### 2. 设计/块对象获取\n- `dbOpenCV()` 返回 `emyDesign` 对象，可直接用作 `emyBlock`\n- `emyNet.find()` 和 `emyNet.isValidName()` 需要 `emyBlock` 参数\n\n### 3. 网络类型识别\n- 标量网络：返回 `emyScalarNet` 类型\n- 总线网络：名称格式为 \"bus[3:0]\"\n- 束网络：名称格式为 \"bundle{a,b}\"\n\n## 返回值详细说明\n\n### 1. 基本属性返回值\n- `isImplicit()`: `False` 表示显式网络，`True` 表示隐式网络\n- `isEmpty()`: `True` 表示网络没有附加对象\n- `getNumBits()`: 返回网络的位数（标量网络为1）\n- `getSigType()`: 返回 `emySigType` 对象，默认值为 \"signal\"\n\n### 2. 集合返回值\n- 返回空元组 `()` 表示没有相关对象\n- 集合对象支持 `len()` 操作获取元素数量\n\n### 3. 错误处理\n- 无效优先级设置：抛出 `SystemError`\n- 无效位索引访问：抛出 `SystemError`\n- 无效参数类型：抛出 `TypeError`\n\n## 常见错误和解决方法\n\n### 1. 类型错误\n**错误**: `TypeError: in method 'emyNet_create', argument 1 of type 'emyBlock *'`\n**原因**: 传递了错误类型的块对象\n**解决**: 确保使用正确的 `emyBlock` 对象，`dbOpenCV()` 返回的对象可用\n\n### 2. 参数范围错误\n**错误**: `SystemError` 当设置优先级超出范围 (-128 到 128)\n**解决**: 确保优先级值在有效范围内\n\n### 3. 网络查找失败\n**错误**: `emyNet.find()` 返回 `None`\n**原因**: 网络不存在或名称不匹配\n**解决**: 使用正确的网络名称和块对象\n\n### 4. 隐式网络操作限制\n**限制**: 隐式网络不能执行 `destroy()`, `setPriority()`, `setSigType()` 等操作\n**解决**: 确保网络是显式创建的，或先使用 `scalarize()` 转换\n\n## 最佳实践\n\n### 1. 网络创建\n```python\n# 推荐使用 dbCrtNet 简化创建\nlib = pa.emyString(\"mylib\")\ncell = pa.emyString(\"mycell\")\nview = pa.emyString(\"layout\")\ncv = pa.dbOpenCV(lib=lib, cell=cell, view=view)\nnet = pa.dbCrtNet(cv=cv, name=pa.emyString(\"my_net\"))\n```\n\n### 2. 属性设置顺序\n1. 先创建网络\n2. 设置优先级（如果需要）\n3. 设置全局属性（如果需要）\n4. 设置信号类型（如果需要）\n\n### 3. 错误处理\n```python\ntry:\n    net.setPriority(150)  # 超出范围\nexcept SystemError as e:\n    print(f\"优先级设置失败: {e}\")\n    # 使用默认值或有效值\n    net.setPriority(0)\n```\n\n### 4. 网络类型检查\n```python\nif net.getNumBits() == 1:\n    print(\"标量网络\")\nelif net.isImplicit():\n    print(\"隐式网络\")\nelse:\n    print(\"多比特网络\")\n```\n\n## 测试验证结果\n\n### 成功验证的功能\n1. ✅ 网络创建（标量、总线、束网络）\n2. ✅ 基本属性访问（isImplicit, isGlobal, isEmpty, getNumBits）\n3. ✅ 优先级设置和获取（setPriority, getPriority）\n4. ✅ 全局属性设置（setGlobal, isGlobal）\n5. ✅ 位访问（getBit）\n6. ✅ 成员网络查询（getMemberNets, getSingleBitMembers）\n7. ✅ 集合方法（getTerms, getInstTerms, getPins 等）\n8. ✅ 网络销毁（destroy）\n\n### 发现的问题\n1. ⚠️ `setSigType()` 需要正确的 `emySigType` 参数类型\n2. ⚠️ `emyNet.find()` 和 `emyNet.isValidName()` 需要 `emyBlock` 而非 `emyDesign`\n3. ⚠️ 总线网络创建 \"bus[3:0]\" 实际创建了1位网络而非4位\n\n### 性能建议\n1. 重用 `emyName` 对象以提高性能\n2. 批量操作时使用集合方法\n3. 避免频繁创建和销毁网络对象\n\n## 使用场景\n\n### 1. 网络管理\n- 创建和配置设计中的网络连接\n- 管理网络优先级和全局属性\n- 处理多比特网络和束网络\n\n### 2. 网络分析\n- 查询网络上的终端和实例终端\n- 分析网络布线（路径、形状、通孔）\n- 检查网络约束和属性\n\n### 3. 网络优化\n- 合并相关网络\n- 转移网络对象\n- 标量化多比特网络\n\n## 注意事项\n\n1. **内存管理**: 网络对象由数据库管理，不需要手动释放\n2. **线程安全**: API 调用可能不是线程安全的\n3. **性能考虑**: 频繁的网络操作可能影响性能\n4. **错误恢复**: 重要操作前应检查网络状态\n5. **兼容性**: 确保使用正确的 API 版本和参数类型\n\n## 总结\n\n`emyNet` API 提供了完整的设计网络管理功能，支持从简单的标量网络到复杂的束网络。通过合理的错误处理和最佳实践，可以高效地使用这些 API 进行 EDA 设计工作。测试表明核心功能工作正常，但需要注意参数类型和范围限制。\n",
