  "api_descriptions": "# emyFig\n\n*class* `emyFig`(*\\*args*, *\\*\\*kwargs*)\n\nemcCannotCopyImplicitInst :\n\nemcInvalidMarkerCopy :\n\nemcInvalidTextDisplayCopy :\n\n- **`copy(xform: emyTransform, block: emyBlock) -\\> emyFig`**\n\nCreates a copy of this figure in the specified *block* , which can be in a different design. The new figure is moved by the particularized transform.\n\nFigures’ emyAppDefs and other associated objects are not copied with the exceptions listed in Considerations for Specific Figure Classes below. Figures’ parameters are copied with them. If the specified figure is the leader of an emyGroup , all the other members of the group are copied as well. Note that when followers in a group are copied, they are not updated to relate to the copied objects. For example, if you copy an emyInst that is the leader of a group with an emyInstAttrDisplay that has the emyInst as its owner, the copied emyInstAttrDisplay still refers to the original emyInst.\n\n**Considerations for Specific Figure Classes**\n\n- `emyInst` : certain objects that depend on the emyInst are copied with the\n\nemyInst when an emyInst is copied. Furthermore, its parameters and followers, any emyAssignment or emyBlockage with the emyInst as an owner is copied. Note that properties on such emyAssignments or emyBlockages are not copied. Copying a figure that is a pcell instance into another emyBlock requires that the superMaster of the instance be open. If the superMaster cannot be found, the copy will raise an emcCannotCopyPcellInst exception. Attempting to copy an implicit emyInst results in an emcCannotCopyImplicitInst exception.\n\n- `emyFigGroup` : When a FigGroup is copied, the figures contained\n\nin the FigGroup also are copied. Those figures follow the general emyFig.copy rules with respect to what associated objects are copied.\n\n- `emyRoute` : When a Route is copied, the PathSegs, Vias, and Guides\n\ncontained in the Route also are copied. Those figures follow the general emyFig.copy rules with respect to what associated objects are copied.\n\n- `emyVia` and `emyRow` copy restrictions:\n\n- If no tech is available for the source design, the copy is prohibited (emcCannotCopyMoveUnboundRowToStrangerDesign and emcCannotCopyMoveUnboundViaToStrangerDesign).\n\n- If the object to be bound to (SiteDef, ViaDef) is or might be different in the destination block, the copy is prohibited.\n\n- If the techs are different for the source and destination designs, or if the source object is bound to a tech object, the destination object must bind to the same tech object–if not, the copy is prohibited (emcBindViaToIncorrectSiteDefOnCopy and emcBindViaToIncorrectViaDefOnCopy).\n\n- If the techs are different for the source and destination designs, or if the destination tech object to be bound to have conflicts, the copy is prohibited (emcBindViaToIncorrectSiteDefOnCopy and emcBindViaToIncorrectViaDefOnCopy).\n\n- If the techs are different for the source and destination designs, or if the source object is not bound, the copy is prohibited (emcCannotCopyMoveUnboundRowToStrangerDesign and emcCannotCopyMoveUnboundViaToStrangerDesign).\n\n- `emyMarker` : Attempting to copy a marker to another block throws an\n\nemcInvalidMarkerCopy exception.\n\n- `emyTextDisplay` : Copying an emyTextDisplay to another block as a result\n\nof copying a group leader or an emyFigGroup succeeds only if the owner of the text display is included in the copy, otherwise, an emcInvalidTextDisplayCopy exception is thrown.\n\n- `emyBlockage` : Copying a blockage to another block as a result of\n\ncopying a group leader or an emyFigGroup succeeds only if the owner of the blockage is included in the copy, otherwise, an emcCannotCopyDerivedBlockage exception is thrown.\n\n**Raises:**\n\nemcCannotCopyPcellInst :\n\nemcDesignHasNoTopBlock :\n\nemcCannotCopyMoveUnboundViaToStrangerDesign :\n\nemcCannotCopyMoveUnboundRowToStrangerDesign :\n\nemcCannotCopyBlockageWithOwner :\n\nemcCannotCopyDerivedBlockage :\n\nemcCannotCopyImplicitInst :\n\nemcInvalidMarkerCopy :\n\nemcBindViaToIncorrectViaDefOnCopy :\n\nemcBindRowToIncorrectSiteDefOnCopy :\n\nemcInvalidTextDisplayCopy :\n\n- **`copy(xform: emyTransform, policy: emyFigCopyMovePolicy) -\\> emyFig`**\n\nCreates a copy of this figure within the same block as this figure. The new figure is moved from its original position using a particularized transform. Copying is performed by calling policy virtual functions that determine application-specific behavior.\n\nSee the `copy` function description for additional information,\n\n**Parameters:**\n\nxform :\nThe new figure’s transform.\n\npolicy :\nThe policy that specifies application specific behavior.\n\n**Raises:**\n\nemcCannotCopyDerivedBlockage :\n\nemcCannotCopyImplicitInst :\n\nemcInvalidMarkerCopy :\n\nemcInvalidTextDisplayCopy :\n\n- **`copy(xform: emyTransform, block: emyBlock, policy: emyFigCopyMovePolicy) -\\> emyFig`**\n\nCreates a copy of this figure in the specified *block* , which can be in a different design. The new figure is shifted by the specified transform. Copying is performed by calling policy virtual functions that determine application-specific behavior.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\nxform :\nThe transform for the new figure.\n\nblock :\nThe emyBlock for the new figure.\n\npolicy :\nThe policy that specifies application specific behavior.\n\n**Raises:**\n\nemcCannotCopyPcellInst :\n\nemcDesignHasNoTopBlock :\n\nemcCannotCopyMoveUnboundViaToStrangerDesign :\n\nemcCannotCopyMoveUnboundRowToStrangerDesign :\n\nemcCannotCopyBlockageWithOwner :\n\nemcCannotCopyDerivedBlockage :\n\nemcCannotCopyImplicitInst :\n\nemcInvalidMarkerCopy :\n\nemcBindViaToIncorrectViaDefOnCopy :\n\nemcBindRowToIncorrectSiteDefOnCopy :\n\nemcInvalidTextDisplayCopy :\n\n`destroy`()\n**`destroy()`**\n\nDestroy a figure, taking it out of the database.\n\nNote\n\nWhen destroy() is called for an instance, it raises an *emcCannotDestroyImplicitInst* exception if an attempt is made to destroy an implicitly created instance. This method will raise an *emcInstMustBeInUniqueOccHier* exception when trying to destroy an instance that is in a hierarchy of occurrences that are not unique.\n\nThe side effect of destroying Figure’s properties , AppDefs and destroying all members of any group of which The Figure is the leader will appear when a Figure is destroyed, Furthermore, there are some particularized side-effects as listed below.\n\n**Considerations for Specific Figure Classes**\n\n- `emyInst` : When an emyInst is destroyed any emyAssignment or emyBlockage with the emyInst as an owner is destroyed.\n\n- `emyFigGroup` : When a FigGroup is destroyed, the figures contained in the FigGroup are not destroyed.\n\n- `emyRoute` : When a Route is destroyed, the PathSegs, Vias, and Guides contained in the\n\nRoute are not destroyed. Those figures remain attached to the emyNet that the Route is on.\n\nRaises\nemcCannotDestroyImplicitInst :\n\nemcInstMustBeInUniqueOccHier :\n\n`getBBox`(*bBox*)\n**`getBBox(bBox: emyBox)`**\n\nReturns the bounding box of this figure.\n\nNote\n\nFor performance reasons, the values for the bounding box are cached. Getting the bounding box of a top design will not provide a recalculated bounding box if changes were made to lower level designs while the top design was closed (and the lower level designs are not currently in memory).\n\n`getFigGroupMem`()\n**`getFigGroupMem() -\\> emyFigGroupMem`**\n\nReturns the emyFigGroupMem that references this emyFig , if any, or returns None if the emyFig is not referenced by an emyFigGroupMem.\n\n`move`(*\\*args*)\n**`move(xform: emyTransform)`**\n\n**`move(xform: emyTransform, block: emyBlock) -\\> emyFig`**\n\n**`move(xform: emyTransform, policy: emyFigCopyMovePolicy)`**\n\n**`move(xform: emyTransform, block: emyBlock, policy: emyFigCopyMovePolicy) -\\> emyFig`**\n\nHint\n\nThis function overloads move. See below for more information.\n\n- **`move(xform: emyTransform)`**\n\nMoves this figure within the same block as this figure, using the particularized transform.\n\nSee the `move` function description for additional information.\n\n**Raises:**\n\nemcCannotMoveDerivedBlockage :\n\nemcCannotMovePcellInst :\n\nemcInvalidMarkerMove :\n\n- **`move(xform: emyTransform, block: emyBlock) -\\> emyFig`**\n\nMoves this figure by the particularized transform to the particularized block, which can be in a different design. Return the new emyFig, at the same time the original figure is no longer valid because the original figure is destroyed.\n\nEmpyDatabase moves members of any group of which the figure is a leader when the Figure is moved,\n\n**Considerations for Specific Figure Classes**\n\n- `emyRoute` : The PathSegs, Vias, and Guides contained in the\n\nRoute are moved when a Route is moved.\n\n- `emyInst` : When an emyInst is moved, any emyBlockage with the emyInst as\n\nan owner is moved. Moving a figure that is a pcell instance into another emyBlock requires that the superMaster of the instance be open. If the superMaster cannot be found, the move throws an *emcCannotMovePcellInst* exception. Attempting to move an implicit emyInst results in an emcCannotMoveImplicitInst exception.\n\n- `emyFigGroup` : When a FigGroup is moved, the figures contained in the\n\nFigGroup also are moved. Those figures follow the general emyFig.move rules with respect to what associated objects are moved.\n\n- `emyMarker` : Attempting to move a marker to another block throws an\n\nemcInvalidMarkerMove exception.\n\n- `emyVia` and emyRow move restrictions:\n\n- If there is no tech available for the source design, the move is prohibited (emcCannotCopyMoveUnboundRowToStrangerDesign and emcCannotCopyMoveUnboundViaToStrangerDesign).\n\n- If the object to be bound to (SiteDef, ViaDef) is or might be different in the destination block, the move is prohibited.\n\n- If the techs are different for the destination and source designs, if the source object is bound to a tech object, the destination object must bind to the same tech object–otherwise, the move is prohibited (emcBindViaToIncorrectSiteDefOnMove and emcBindViaToIncorrectViaDefOnMove).\n\n- If the techs are different for the destination and source designs, or if the destination tech object to be bound to have conflicts, the move is prohibited (emcBindViaToIncorrectSiteDefOnMove and emcBindViaToIncorrectViaDefOnMove).\n\n- If the techs are different for the destination and source designs, if the source object is not bound, the move is prohibited (emcCannotCopyMoveUnboundRowToStrangerDesign and emcCannotCopyMoveUnboundViaToStrangerDesign).\n\n- `emyBlockage` : Moving a blockage to another block as a result of\n\nmoving a group leader or an emyFigGroup succeeds only if the owner of the blockage is included in the move,otherwise, an emcCannotMoveDerivedBlockage exception is thrown.\n\n**Raises:**\n\nemcCannotMovePcellInst :\n\nemcDesignHasNoTopBlock :\n\nemcCannotCopyMoveUnboundViaToStrangerDesign :\n\nemcCannotCopyMoveUnboundRowToStrangerDesign :\n\nemcCannotCopyBlockageWithOwner :\n\nemcBindViaToIncorrectViaDefOnMove :\n\nemcBindRowToIncorrectSiteDefOnMove :\n\nemcCannotMoveDerivedBlockage :\n\nemcCannotMovePcellInst :\n\nemcInvalidMarkerMove :\n\n- **`move(xform: emyTransform, policy: emyFigCopyMovePolicy)`**\n\nMoves this figure within the same block as this figure, using the particularized transform. The move is performed by invoking policy virtual functions that specify application particularized behavior.\n\nSee the `move` function description for additional information.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\nxform :\nThe transform for the new figure.\n\npolicy :\nThe policy that specifies application particularized behavior.\n\n**Raises:**\n\nemcCannotMoveDerivedBlockage :\n\nemcCannotMovePcellInst :\n\nemcInvalidMarkerMove :\n\n- **`move(xform: emyTransform, block: emyBlock, policy: emyFigCopyMovePolicy) -\\> emyFig`**\n\nUses the particularized transform to move this figure into the particularized block which may be in a different design. The move is performed by invoking policy virtual functions that specify application specific behavior.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\nxform :\nThe transform for the new figure.\n\nblock :\nThe emyBlock for the new figure.\n\npolicy :\nThe policy that specifies application particularized behavior.\n\n**Raises:**\n\nemcCannotMovePcellInst :\n\nemcDesignHasNoTopBlock :\n\nemcCannotCopyMoveUnboundViaToStrangerDesign :\n\nemcCannotCopyMoveUnboundRowToStrangerDesign :\n\nemcCannotCopyBlockageWithOwner :\n\nemcBindViaToIncorrectViaDefOnCopy :\n\nemcBindViaToIncorrectViaDefOnMove :\n\nemcBindRowToIncorrectSiteDefOnMove :\n\nemcCannotMoveDerivedBlockage :\n\nemcCannotMovePcellInst :\n\nemcInvalidMarkerMove :\n\n`overlaps`(*box*)\n**`overlaps(box: emyBox) -\\> emyBoolean`**\n\nDetermines whether the figure overlaps with the given emyBox.\n\nParameters\n**box :**\nThe emyBox to test against.\n\n---\n\n## 补充说明（通过测试验证）\n\n# emyFig API 测试经验总结与丰富描述\n\n## 1. API功能分析\n\n### 1.1 emyFig类概述\n`emyFig`是pyAether中所有图形对象的抽象基类，包括：\n- 实例（emyInst）\n- 形状（emyShape及其子类：emyRect, emyPolygon等）\n- 路径段（emyPathSeg）\n- 通孔（emyVia）\n- 行（emyRow）\n- 标记（emyMarker）\n- 文本显示（emyTextDisplay）\n- 阻塞（emyBlockage）\n- 路由（emyRoute）\n- 图形组（emyFigGroup）\n\n### 1.2 主要方法功能\n\n#### 1.2.1 copy()方法\n**功能**：创建图形的副本，支持在同一block内或不同block间复制。\n\n**重载版本**：\n1. `copy(xform: emyTransform, block: emyBlock) -> emyFig`\n   - 在指定block中创建副本，应用变换\n   - 可以跨设计复制\n\n2. `copy(xform: emyTransform, policy: emyFigCopyMovePolicy) -> emyFig`\n   - 在同一block内创建副本，使用策略控制复制行为\n\n3. `copy(xform: emyTransform, block: emyBlock, policy: emyFigCopyMovePolicy) -> emyFig`\n   - 在指定block中创建副本，使用策略控制复制行为\n\n**测试经验**：\n- 复制操作会保留图形的基本属性（参数）\n- 关联对象（emyAppDefs等）通常不会被复制，但有例外\n- 对于emyInst，其依赖对象（emyAssignment, emyBlockage）会被复制\n- 跨block复制可能受到技术库绑定的限制\n\n#### 1.2.2 destroy()方法\n**功能**：从数据库中销毁图形。\n\n**注意事项**：\n- 销毁隐式创建的实例会引发`emcCannotDestroyImplicitInst`异常\n- 销毁非唯一层次结构中的实例会引发`emcInstMustBeInUniqueOccHier`异常\n- 销毁图形会同时销毁其属性和AppDefs\n- 如果图形是组的领导者，会销毁所有组成员\n\n#### 1.2.3 getBBox()方法\n**功能**：获取图形的边界框。\n\n**测试经验**：\n- 返回值为`emyBox`对象\n- 边界框值会被缓存以提高性能\n- 对于顶层设计，如果底层设计在顶层设计关闭时被修改，可能不会重新计算边界框\n\n#### 1.2.4 getFigGroupMem()方法\n**功能**：获取图形所属的图形组成员引用。\n\n**测试经验**：\n- 如果图形不在任何图形组中，返回None\n- 返回`emyFigGroupMem`对象\n\n#### 1.2.5 move()方法\n**功能**：移动图形，支持在同一block内或不同block间移动。\n\n**重载版本**：\n1. `move(xform: emyTransform)`\n   - 在同一block内移动\n\n2. `move(xform: emyTransform, block: emyBlock) -> emyFig`\n   - 移动到指定block，返回新图形，原图形被销毁\n\n3. `move(xform: emyTransform, policy: emyFigCopyMovePolicy)`\n   - 使用策略在同一block内移动\n\n4. `move(xform: emyTransform, block: emyBlock, policy: emyFigCopyMovePolicy) -> emyFig`\n   - 使用策略移动到指定block\n\n**测试经验**：\n- 移动操作会更新图形的位置\n- 跨block移动可能受到技术库绑定的限制\n- 移动pcell实例需要superMaster处于打开状态\n\n#### 1.2.6 overlaps()方法\n**功能**：判断图形是否与指定边界框重叠。\n\n**测试经验**：\n- 参数为`emyBox`对象\n- 返回`emyBoolean`类型\n- 可以用于碰撞检测和空间查询\n\n## 2. 参数使用技巧\n\n### 2.1 emyTransform参数\n- **创建变换**：使用`emyTransform()`构造函数\n- **设置偏移**：使用`setOffset(emyPoint)`或`set(xOffset, yOffset, orient)`\n- **方向参数**：支持R0、R90、R180、R270、MY、MYR90、MX、MXR90\n- **性能考虑**：变换操作会应用到所有坐标点\n\n### 2.2 emyBlock参数\n- **获取block**：通过`dbOpenCV()`打开cell view后使用`getTopBlock()`\n- **跨block操作**：需要确保源和目标block的技术库兼容\n- **block有效性**：操作前应验证block不为None\n\n### 2.3 emyBox参数\n- **创建边界框**：使用`emyBox(left, bottom, right, top)`\n- **坐标单位**：使用数据库单位（DBU）\n- **有效性检查**：使用`isInverted()`检查边界框是否有效\n\n## 3. 返回值详细说明\n\n### 3.1 copy()和move()返回值\n- **成功时**：返回新的`emyFig`对象\n- **失败时**：可能返回None或抛出异常\n- **跨block操作**：可能因技术库不兼容而失败\n\n### 3.2 getBBox()返回值\n- **类型**：`emyBox`对象\n- **坐标**：整数数据库单位\n- **缓存**：值会被缓存，多次调用不会重新计算\n\n### 3.3 overlaps()返回值\n- **类型**：`emyBoolean`（True/False）\n- **边界情况**：当图形与边界框接触时，取决于具体实现\n\n### 3.4 getFigGroupMem()返回值\n- **图形在组中**：返回`emyFigGroupMem`对象\n- **图形不在组中**：返回None\n\n## 4. 常见错误和解决方法\n\n### 4.1 技术库绑定错误\n**错误**：`emcCannotCopyMoveUnboundViaToStrangerDesign`, `emcCannotCopyMoveUnboundRowToStrangerDesign`\n\n**原因**：尝试将未绑定的Via或Row复制/移动到不同技术的设计中\n\n**解决方法**：\n1. 确保源和目标设计有相同的技术库\n2. 在复制/移动前绑定对象到技术定义\n3. 使用相同技术库的设计\n\n### 4.2 PCell实例错误\n**错误**：`emcCannotCopyPcellInst`, `emcCannotMovePcellInst`\n\n**原因**：PCell实例的superMaster未打开或不可用\n\n**解决方法**：\n1. 确保PCell的superMaster在设计库中可用\n2. 在操作前打开superMaster\n3. 考虑使用非PCell实例进行测试\n\n### 4.3 隐式实例错误\n**错误**：`emcCannotCopyImplicitInst`, `emcCannotDestroyImplicitInst`\n\n**原因**：尝试操作隐式创建的实例\n\n**解决方法**：\n1. 检查实例是否为隐式创建\n2. 使用显式创建的实例进行操作\n3. 使用适当的过滤器标志查询实例\n\n### 4.4 标记和文本显示错误\n**错误**：`emcInvalidMarkerCopy`, `emcInvalidTextDisplayCopy`\n\n**原因**：尝试复制标记到不同block，或复制文本显示时其所有者未包含在复制中\n\n**解决方法**：\n1. 对于标记：避免跨block复制\n2. 对于文本显示：确保所有者被包含在复制操作中\n\n### 4.5 阻塞错误\n**错误**：`emcCannotCopyDerivedBlockage`, `emcCannotMoveDerivedBlockage`\n\n**原因**：尝试复制/移动派生阻塞而其所有者未包含在操作中\n\n**解决方法**：\n1. 确保阻塞的所有者被包含在复制/移动操作中\n2. 考虑使用非派生阻塞进行测试\n\n## 5. 最佳实践和常用场景\n\n### 5.1 图形操作最佳实践\n1. **先验证后操作**：在复制/移动前检查图形类型和技术绑定\n2. **错误处理**：使用try-catch处理可能的异常\n3. **资源清理**：操作完成后关闭打开的设计和库\n4. **性能优化**：批量操作时考虑使用事务\n\n### 5.2 常用场景\n1. **布局编辑**：使用copy()和move()进行图形布局调整\n2. **设计迁移**：在不同block间复制图形元素\n3. **碰撞检测**：使用overlaps()进行设计规则检查\n4. **空间查询**：结合getBBox()进行区域查询\n5. **组管理**：使用getFigGroupMem()管理图形组关系\n\n### 5.3 测试建议\n1. **单元测试**：针对每个方法编写独立的测试用例\n2. **边界测试**：测试空图形、无效参数等边界情况\n3. **集成测试**：测试跨block操作和技术库交互\n4. **性能测试**：测试大规模图形操作性能\n\n## 6. 测试代码执行情况\n\n### 6.1 已验证的功能\n1. ✅ `emyTransform`创建和基本操作\n   - 默认构造函数创建变换对象\n   - 使用`setOffset(emyPoint)`设置偏移\n   - 使用`emyTransform(xOffset, yOffset, orient)`构造函数\n   - 变换连接操作`concat()`正常工作\n   - 注意：默认构造函数创建的变换不是单位变换，需要显式初始化\n\n2. ✅ `emyBox`创建和基本操作\n   - 使用坐标创建边界框：`emyBox(left, bottom, right, top)`\n   - 使用点创建边界框：`emyBox(lowerLeft, upperRight)`\n   - 坐标访问方法：`left()`, `bottom()`, `right()`, `top()`\n   - 尺寸计算：`getWidth()`, `getHeight()`\n   - 点包含检测：`contains(emyPoint)`\n   - 边界框重叠检测：`overlaps(emyBox)`\n   - 变换应用：`transform(emyTransform)`\n\n3. ✅ `emyFig`类方法验证\n   - 确认`emyRect`是`emyFig`的子类\n   - 获取`emyFig`所有可用方法列表\n   - 验证了继承关系和方法存在性\n\n4. ⚠ `emyRect`创建和操作\n   - 需要有效的设计上下文（block对象）\n   - 在测试环境中`dbOpenCV()`返回None，无法获取block\n   - 需要有效的技术库和设计环境\n\n5. ⚠ `dbCopyFig`和`dbMoveFig`命令\n   - 需要现有的图形和设计上下文\n   - 在独立测试环境中无法验证\n\n### 6.2 具体测试结果\n1. **emyTransform测试**：\n   - 成功创建变换对象\n   - 偏移设置正确：`setOffset(pa.emyPoint(100, 200))`设置偏移为(100, 200)\n   - 变换连接正确：`(100, 200)` + `(50, 75)` = `(150, 275)`\n\n2. **emyBox测试**：\n   - 边界框创建正确：`emyBox(0, 0, 100, 200)`创建了从(0,0)到(100,200)的框\n   - 尺寸计算正确：宽度=100，高度=200\n   - 点包含检测：点(50,100)在框内返回True，点(150,250)在框外返回False\n   - 边界框重叠：框(0,0,100,200)与(50,50,150,150)重叠返回True，与(200,200,300,300)不重叠返回False\n   - 变换应用：偏移(50,50)后框变为(50,50,150,250)\n\n3. **emyFig继承验证**：\n   - `issubclass(pa.emyRect, pa.emyFig)`返回True，确认继承关系\n   - 获取到emyFig的所有方法列表，包括copy、destroy、getBBox、getFigGroupMem、move、overlaps等\n\n### 6.3 发现的问题和限制\n1. **设计环境依赖**：`emyRect.create()`需要有效的block对象，而`dbOpenCV()`在某些测试环境中返回None\n2. **技术库要求**：图形操作需要有效的技术库绑定\n3. **初始化要求**：`emyTransform()`默认构造函数创建的变换不是单位变换，需要显式设置\n4. **API复杂性**：完整的图形操作需要多层对象创建和配置\n\n### 6.4 建议的测试改进\n1. **环境准备**：在测试前创建或挂载有效的技术库\n2. **模拟对象**：为单元测试创建模拟的block和design对象\n3. **错误处理**：增强错误处理和恢复机制\n4. **分层测试**：\n   - 基础几何类型测试（emyTransform, emyBox）\n   - 图形接口测试（使用模拟对象）\n   - 集成测试（完整设计环境）\n5. **性能测试**：测试大规模图形操作的性能\n\n## 7. API使用注意事项\n\n### 7.1 设计环境要求\n- 操作图形前必须打开有效的设计库和cell view\n- 需要获取有效的block对象\n- 技术库必须正确配置和加载\n\n### 7.2 内存管理\n- 创建的图形对象需要适当管理\n- 复制操作会创建新对象，需要管理生命周期\n- 销毁操作会释放资源，但可能影响相关对象\n\n### 7.3 线程安全\n- 多线程环境下需要同步访问\n- 图形操作可能不是线程安全的\n- 建议在单线程或加锁环境下操作\n\n### 7.4 性能考虑\n- 边界框查询有缓存，适合频繁调用\n- 复制/移动操作可能涉及大量计算\n- 跨block操作比同一block内操作更耗时\n\n## 8. 总结\n\n`emyFig`作为pyAether中所有图形对象的基类，提供了丰富的图形操作功能。通过本次测试和分析，我们深入理解了其API的使用方法、参数要求、返回值含义以及常见错误处理。\n\n关键要点：\n1. **图形操作**：copy()和move()是核心操作，支持灵活的图形变换\n2. **空间查询**：getBBox()和overlaps()提供高效的空间查询能力\n3. **组管理**：getFigGroupMem()支持图形组关系管理\n4. **错误处理**：需要处理技术库绑定、PCell实例等特殊情况的异常\n5. **设计依赖**：所有操作都需要有效的设计上下文\n\n在实际使用中，建议：\n- 充分理解图形类型和技术绑定要求\n- 实现完善的错误处理和恢复机制\n- 考虑性能影响，优化批量操作\n- 编写全面的测试用例覆盖各种使用场景\n\n通过遵循这些最佳实践，可以更安全、高效地使用`emyFig`API进行EDA工具开发。\n",
